window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS=(window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":251,"title":"Chapter 251: A human?","paragraphs":["Tap.","Tap.","Soft footsteps echoed along the wooden corridor.","Each step was calm and slow. Neither cautious nor hostile.","Noah stood quietly in the middle of the room, his muscles tense despite his attempt to appear relaxed.","The footsteps stopped. A figure appeared at the doorway.","Noah’s breathing caught for a brief moment. Standing before him was a an extremely beautiful woman.","She stood six feet tall, her posture elegant and perfectly composed.","A traditional kimono of deep blue and black wrapped gracefully around her figure. A wide obi was tied neatly around her waist, emphasizing her slender frame before flowing naturally over her wide hips.","Her skin was smooth and porcelain fair. But what immediately drew Noah’s attention. It wasn’t her beauty. It was her neck.","Dark sapphire-blue scales covered both sides of it, extending upward beneath her chin. A few smaller scales reached her right cheek, blending naturally with her flawless skin.","Despite their unusual appearance. They somehow didn’t lessen her beauty.","Instead they gave her an almost mystical aura.","Her long raven-black hair was tied into an elegant bun, secured by a crystal-blue hairpin that shimmered softly whenever it caught the morning light.","A small beauty mark rested beneath the corner of her right eye. Her face appeared to belong to a woman around thirty years old.","Yet the depth hidden within her sharp blue eyes suggested someone far older.","Those eyes, Noah unconsciously stiffened.","’Vertical pupils...’","They weren’t human. Her irises possessed narrow vertical slits, much like the eyes of demons. Yet she didn’t look like a demon at all. She didn’t possess any horns.","She simply stood there. Calmly observing him.","\"...Uhm...\"","Noah scratched the back of his head awkwardly.","\"Hello?\"","The woman didn’t respond. Her emotionless gaze continued studying him from head to toe. Silence lingered between them.","\"...Hello, ma’am?\"","Noah tried once more.","The instant his words reached her. Her eyes widened.","\"...A...\"","Her lips parted slightly.","\"...Human?\"","There was unmistakable disbelief in her voice.","Noah blinked. \"Well...\"","He gave an awkward smile. \"I am human.\"","The moment those words left his mouth. Her composed expression completely shattered. Her eyes widened even further.","Before Noah could react she vanished.","No. She hadn’t teleported. She had simply moved so fast that his eyes couldn’t follow her.","\"...!\"","She appeared directly in front of him. Both hands immediately reached out. Soft palms gently cupped his cheeks.","Before Noah could even process what was happening... She tilted his face upward.","Then downward. Then to the left. Then to the right.","She inspected him from every possible angle as though verifying something unbelievably precious.","Noah stood completely frozen. The warmth of her hands contrasted with the cool morning air.","They were surprisingly soft. Those palms were smooth and delicate.","\"A human...\"","Her voice trembled ever so slightly.","\"...A real human.\"","There was excitement hidden beneath her usually calm tone.","No more than excitement. It sounded like someone witnessing a miracle they had long ago given up believing would ever happen.","For several long seconds. She simply stared into Noah’s face.","Only after noticing his increasingly awkward expression did she finally realize how close she was standing.","\"...\"","She slowly released his cheeks. Taking a single step backward, she closed her eyes and drew a slow breath.","When she opened them again. Her usual calm expression had returned. Only a faint trace of excitement still lingered deep within her eyes.","She looked directly at Noah.","\"Young man...What is your name? Who are you? And...How did you come to this place?\"","Noah straightened his posture.","\"My name is Noah Eldritch.\"","He gave a polite bow.","\"As for how I arrived here...\"","He let out a helpless laugh.","\"It’s... a rather long story.\"","For just an instant. The corners of the woman’s lips twitched upward. As though she were struggling to suppress a smile.","\"I have all the time in the world.\"","Her voice was little gentle. \"I would be more than happy to hear it.\"","She paused before adding quietly, \"It has been a very long time since I last met another person.\"","Noah’s eyes flickered slightly.","’Another person...? Does that mean... She’s been living here alone this entire time?","The thought immediately raised countless questions. Who was she? How long had she been here?","And... Was she trapped here just like him?","Realizing he had been staring blankly, Noah quickly asked,","\"May I know your name, ma’am?\"","The woman blinked once before letting out a soft sigh.","\"Oh... I completely forgot. How rude of me.\"","She placed one hand lightly over her chest.","\"My name is Akari Narukami.\"","Her voice carried quiet elegance.","\"You may simply call me Akari.\"","She looked at Noah with a faint, almost imperceptible smile.","\"Welcome...to my home.\"","---","A little while later...","Noah and Akari sat together in the open room overlooking the peaceful garden.","The morning breeze drifted gently through the open sliding doors, carrying the fresh scent of rain-soaked grass.","Akari sat gracefully in seiza, folding both legs neatly beneath her as she rested her weight upon her heels. Her back remained perfectly straight, her hands resting elegantly upon her lap.","Every movement she made was calm, controlled and almost effortless.","Noah watched her for a moment before awkwardly attempting to imitate the same posture. \"Like this?\"","He adjusted his legs slightly before finally settling into position. It wasn’t exactly comfortable.","Still he managed.","’She really looks elegant. Like someone born into nobility. Every movement she makes is refined.’","His eyes unconsciously drifted downward. Near the entrance of the room rested her traditional wooden sandals.","’Those are... Eastern-style wooden sandals.’","Noah’s thoughts wandered briefly.","’I often compare them to old Japanese traditions... But in this world, those customs originated from the Eastern Duchy. The Raiko Dukedom. and Her surname Narukami.’","Combined with her appearance... He had already begun forming a guess.","Still he chose not to ask immediately. Instead he began explaining everything that had happened.","From entering the labyrinth alongside Damien. To defeating the giant guardian. The mysterious portal. And finally awakening beside the lake before eventually discovering this secluded house.","As he spoke, Akari quietly listened without interrupting. Between them rested two simple wooden cups.","The drink she had prepared resembled tea, though Noah had never tasted anything quite like it before. It possessed a gentle herbal fragrance with a slightly sweet aftertaste.","\"This is good.\"","He took another sip.","\"What is it?\"","Akari answered softly.","\"I made it from the leaves that grow nearby. They help calm the mind.\"","Noah gave an appreciative nod. By the time his story ended.","His cup was completely empty.","Akari quietly looked out toward the peaceful garden for several moments.","Finally she nodded.","\"I understand. So that’s how you arrived here.\"","She slowly turned her gaze toward Noah.","Their eyes met. \"You said your name is Noah Eldritch.\"","He nodded.","\"Yes.\"","A moment of silence followed. Then she asked, \"Who is your father?\"","Noah blinked. \"You know the Eldritch family?\"","Akari answered without hesitation.","\"Of course I do.\"","Noah’s thoughts immediately raced.","’Then... She really is from the outside world. And judging by her surname... She’s actually from House Narukami. But how? Did she also arrive here through a labyrinth...?’","Pushing those thoughts aside for the moment, he answered her question.","\"My father’s name is Julian Eldritch.\"","The instant those words left his mouth.","Akari frowned. \"Julian Eldritch...\"","She quietly repeated the name to herself. Then her blue eyes widened slightly.","\"Then....You’re that Noah?\""]},{"number":252,"title":"Chapter 252: Akari [1]","paragraphs":["Noah looked puzzled.","\"That Noah? What do you mean?\"","Instead of answering. Akari leaned forward slightly. Her usually calm expression had completely disappeared. For the first time since they met. Genuine emotion appeared on her face.","\"Tell me...\" Her voice carried unmistakable urgency.","\"Is your mother’s name...Catylen?\"","Noah’s eyes widened.","\"Yes.\"","He stared at her in complete disbelief. \"How do you know my mother? And...\"","Unable to contain his curiosity any longer, he asked,","\"Are you... from the Narukami family? The ducal family that rules the Eastern Raigamine Dukedom?\"","Akari immediately nodded.","\"Yes. My father is Reiji Narukami.\"","Silence.","Noah simply stared at her. His thoughts came to a complete halt.","’Reiji Narukami...? Then...That would make her...’","His heart skipped a beat.","’No way.’","Before he could even organize his thoughts. Akari spoke first. Her brows were tightly knitted. \"...But that doesn’t make any sense.\"","She looked directly into Noah’s eyes. \"Why are you so young?\"","Noah blinked. \"What? What do you mean?\"","Akari slowly shook her head.","\"I knew Julian. I knew him since he was young. We are of a similar age before I found myself here.\"","She looked down at her own hands. Then quietly continued,","\"I’ve been trapped in this place...For sixty years.\"","She looked back at Noah.","\"If you’re Julian’s son...You should have only been seven or eight years old before I disappeared.\"","She paused. Her voice grew quieter.","\"So...How are you sitting here before me as a young man barely twenty years old?\"","The room fell silent. Noah’s pupils slowly contracted.","Then everything clicked into place. His thoughts raced.","’Time... Time flows differently here. Much differently than in the outside world.’","A chill ran down his spine.","He slowly raised his eyes toward Akari. Realization struck him. One that was really shocking.","’Akari Narukami...who is stuck here for Sixty years. Daughter of Reiji Narukami...’","His breathing unconsciously slowed. ’She’s... Ophelia’s mother. The woman everyone believed died twelve years ago.’","But now she was sitting calmly before him. Not exactly calmly anymore.","---","Silence lingered between them.","Only the gentle breeze drifting through the open veranda and the soft chirping of birds outside disturbed the peaceful room.","Neither Noah nor Akari spoke. Both were still trying to process what they had just learned.","After a long moment Noah finally broke the silence. \"I think the time—\"","\"The flow of time here is different.\" Akari quietly finished his sentence before he could.","She let out a soft sigh. \"Time moves much faster here than it does in the outside world.\"","Her gaze drifted toward the garden beyond the veranda.","\"One year in outside world...is approximately five years here.\"","Noah slowly nodded. \"So my guess was right.\"","Everything suddenly made much more sense.","Countless questions immediately surfaced in his mind.","’How did she end up here? Was she pulled in through a labyrinth like I was? What are those blue scales on her neck? And those eyes. They’re unlike any human’s.’","They resembled the vertical pupils of demons. The mystery surrounding her only deepened.","Still Noah chose not to ask. They had only just met. Some questions could wait.","Instead he quietly decided to let Akari ask whatever she wished first.","After all she had spent sixty years trapped in this place. Compared to his confusion, her curiosity must have been immeasurably greater.","Akari remained silent. Then, almost hesitantly she looked at Noah.","\"How is my family?\"","Her voice had become much quieter. \"Do you know anything about them?\"","A brief pause followed. Then she asked the question she had clearly wanted to ask from the very beginning.","\"What about my daughter?Ophelia... How is she?\"","Her blue eyes searched Noah’s face anxiously.","\"You should know her. You grew up around the same time.\"","Noah hesitated.","He did possess the memories of the original Noah. But those memories of Akari herself were vague.","Blurry. He had been too young when she disappeared.","Besides. The woman sitting before him looked very different from the fragments preserved in those childhood memories. Far more composed.","And far more intimidating. And far more beautiful.","After gathering his thoughts, Noah answered honestly. \"I don’t know much about Lord Reiji. I’m afraid I can’t tell you how he’s doing.\"","He offered an apologetic smile.","\"But... I do know Ophelia.\"","A faint warmth appeared in Akari’s eyes.","Noah continued,","\"She’s doing well. We’re about the same age now. And...\"","He couldn’t help giving a small, awkward laugh.","\"She’s grown into an incredibly beautiful woman. She’s also talented. And she is really doing good in Novaris Academy.\"","The words left his mouth but inwardly. Noah felt as though his stomach had tied itself into knots.","’Why am I praising her...? If she were standing here right now, we’d probably start arguing within five minutes.’","Their relationship had never been particularly friendly since that incident. If anything it was far more complicated.","Still looking into the hopeful eyes of the woman before him... He simply couldn’t bring himself to say anything negative.","’Maybe. Once I get to know Akari better. I’ll tell her the full story. Including every ridiculous thing her daughter has done.’","That thought made him smile inwardly.","Akari, however, seemed not to notice. The moment she heard Noah speak about Ophelia...","Her eyes trembled. She slowly lowered her head. Her fingers tightened around the fabric of her kimono resting upon her lap.","As though desperately holding onto decades-old memories.","\"She’s... already a young woman...\"","Her voice shook ever so slightly. A faint layer of moisture gathered in her eyes.","\"Oh...\"","She gave a quiet, almost disbelieving laugh.","\"I truly thought...I’d never hear anything about her again. I believed that even if I somehow escaped this place...she would already be gone. That I would never see her again. But there is still hope.\"","A single tear escaped before she quietly wiped it away with the sleeve of her kimono.","She took a slow, steady breath.","Gradually the composure she had carried since meeting Noah returned.","Yet this time there was unmistakable hope within her eyes.","She looked directly at him.","\"Noah.\"","A faint smile finally appeared on her face.","\"I want to hear more. Tell me everything you know about Ophelia. Anything at all.\"","Her voice carried a quiet excitement. Like a mother trying to make up for sixty years of lost time. Noah looked at her for a long moment before letting out a helpless smile.","\"I suppose. It’s going to be a long conversation.\""]},{"number":253,"title":"Chapter 253: Akari [2]","paragraphs":["The conversation continued for quite some time.","Noah told Akari everything he knew about Ophelia. Or at least, everything he thought she wanted to hear.","He spoke about Ophelia’s achievements at the academy, her exceptional talent, her strength, and the respect she had earned from others.","Of course he conveniently left out every argument they had ever had. In fact, he found himself exaggerating some of her better qualities.","’I seriously can’t believe I’m praising her this much... If Ophelia ever hears this, she’ll probably become even more arrogant.’","Still seeing the happiness gradually return to Akari’s face, Noah felt it was worth it. He was a man after all. If a beautiful milf- no, a beautiful lady like Akari could smile because of him then he was happy.","Eventually, the conversation shifted.","He carefully brought up Lionel Thornveil.","Or rather. \"The former Duke Thornveil,\" as Noah privately preferred to think of him.","When he finished explaining everything he knew, Akari simply lowered her gaze and nodded.","\"So...Lionel remarried.\"","Her voice remained calm. There wasn’t the slightest trace of surprise. Nor bitterness.","Noah blinked. \"...That’s it?\"","Akari looked back at him.","He hesitated before asking, \"Aren’t you... angry? Or at least a little sad?\"","Akari smiled faintly and slowly shook her head.","\"No. Our marriage was arranged from the very beginning. It was an alliance between two ducal families. Nothing more.\"","She spoke without resentment.","Almost as though she were simply recalling an old historical fact.","\"Lionel and I respected each other. But...We never truly loved one another as husband and wife should. So...I can’t blame him for choosing to move forward after everyone believed I had died.\"","She looked toward the garden.","\"If anything... I’m relieved he didn’t spend his entire life trapped in the past.\"","Noah quietly nodded. He wasn’t particularly surprised. Political marriages among great noble houses were common.","Love was often a luxury rather than a requirement. With that topic finished.","Noah finally leaned forward slightly.","\"Akari. May I ask you a few questions now?\"","Akari, who still wore a gentle smile after hearing about Ophelia, looked at him and nodded.","\"Of course.I expected you would.\"","Her fingertips lightly brushed the blue scales along her neck.","\"Especially after seeing... this.\"","A faint smile appeared on her lips.","\"I imagine my appearance has raised quite a few questions.\"","Noah nodded honestly.","\"There are... several things I’m curious about.\"","He organized his thoughts before asking the question that bothered him the most.","\"How did you end up here? Were you pulled into this place through a labyrinth like I was?\"","He paused briefly.","\"As far as everyone in the outside world knows....you died during the demon invasion of House Thornveil.\"","Akari remained silent for several seconds.","Then she slowly shook her head.","\"No. I didn’t arrive here the same way you did.\"","She lowered her gaze.","\"It would be more accurate to say...someone brought me here. And trapped me here.\"","Noah’s pupils contracted.","’Someone...?’","His mind immediately began racing.","’Someone powerful enough to imprison a Duchess... Who could possibly do that?’","Akari continued before he could interrupt.","\"I still don’t know why the demons attacked House Thornveil. It made no sense. The residence of a Duke is one of the most heavily defended places in the Empire. For demons to launch such an assault...was both incredibly reckless and unbelievably daring.\"","Her eyes gradually darkened as old memories resurfaced.","\"But...They weren’t ordinary demons. They were among the highest-ranking demons I had ever encountered. Their strength exceeded anything we had anticipated.\"","She slowly clenched one hand.","\"Even Lionel, his father and I who were strongest...struggled against them.\"","A brief silence followed.","\"In the end...I managed to kill one of them. But the battle pushed me beyond my limits.\"","Her fingers gently traced the sapphire-blue scales on her neck.","\"It was during that fight...that my bloodline awakened.\"","Noah instinctively looked toward the scales.","\"...A bloodline? What kind of bloodline?\"","Akari stared quietly into the distance.","When she finally answered. Her voice was calm. Yet carried unmistakable pride.","\"The bloodline of a dragon.\"","She paused.","\"A Storm Dragon. A dragon that governs lightning and storms.\"","Noah’s brain stopped functioning for several seconds.","’D-Dragon...? What the hell?!’","He stared at her in complete disbelief.","\"W-Wait! So...Does that mean... You’re actually a dragon now? Not a human?\"","Akari couldn’t help smiling at his reaction. She softly shook her head.","\"No. Not entirely. My bloodline only awakened partially. I’m still fundamentally human. The dragon blood merely transformed parts of my body.\"","She touched the scales on her neck once more.","\"I’ve spent the last sixty years training. Learning to control its power. And attempting to awaken it completely.\"","A quiet determination appeared in her eyes.","\"I believe... I’m very close.\"","Noah slowly pieced everything together.","Then another memory surfaced. The storm. The rain. The terrifying silhouette hidden among the thunderclouds.","His eyes widened.","\"...Wait. Last night’s storm...\"","He pointed outside.","\"Don’t tell me...\"","Akari gave him an apologetic smile.","\"...Yes. I created it.\"","She lowered her head slightly.","\"I’m sorry. My training caused you unnecessary trouble.\"","Noah’s jaw slowly dropped. He remembered the violent winds that had shaken the forest.","The endless lightning. The massive tornado that stretched into the heavens.","And those enormous glowing blue eyes watching him from within the clouds.","He swallowed hard.","\"...Then...The gigantic shadow I saw inside the storm....was that also you?\"","Akari nodded without hesitation.","\"Yes.\"","A faint smile appeared on her face. \"That...was my dragon form which I am still struggling to use perfectly.\"","The room fell silent.","Noah simply stared at her. His mind replayed the image from the previous night. The colossal silhouette hidden within the storm clouds. The brilliant lightning illuminating eyes.","Those enormous glowing eyes. A chill ran down his spine.","’So... I spent the entire night only a few kilometers away from a dragon... No wonder that storm felt like the end of the world. But now I am sitting beside the same dragon.’"]},{"number":254,"title":"Chapter 254: Akari [3]","paragraphs":["Noah took a slow, steady breath, allowing himself to recover from the shock.","A dragon. A real dragon bloodline stood before him. After calming himself, he asked the question that had been lingering in his mind from the beginning.","\"Then who brought you here?\"","The instant those words left his mouth. Akari’s expression grew noticeably more serious. She lowered her eyes, as though recalling a memory she had buried deep within her heart.","\"To be honest I don’t know much about him.\"","She spoke slowly, carefully choosing each word.","\"During the battle against the demons, I fought one of their commanders. His name was Rashkir. The battle lasted for hours. He was unbelievably powerful.\"","Akari unconsciously clenched one hand.","\"In the end, we both unleashed our strongest attacks. Our final clash...created an enormous explosion.\"","She paused for a brief moment.","\"Rashkir died. I survived. But before I could even understand what had happened... A portal suddenly appeared out of nowhere. It swallowed me before I had any chance to resist.\"","She looked toward the garden outside.","\"When I regained consciousness... I was already here.\"","Her fingers lightly tightened around the fabric of her kimono.","\"And then...I heard a voice.\"","Noah quietly listened.","\"It wasn’t loud. But it carried an overwhelming pressure. It felt...\"","She searched for the proper words.","\"Absolute. As though the very world itself was speaking.\"","A faint chill passed through Noah.","\"What did it say?\"","Akari slowly answered,","\"It told me that I had been chosen to become the next Dragon of Storm and Lightning. It said I was to remain here, train and awaken the dragon bloodline completely. And only after achieving that...would I be allowed to leave.\"","Noah stared at her.","\"That’s it? No explanation? No reason? And who that voice belong to?\"","Akari slowly shook her head.","\"I asked the same questions.\"","She met Noah’s eyes.","\"The only answer it gave me was that it was a dragon. A being like me. A dragon.\"","She paused.","\"After that... I never heard its voice again. That was first and last time.\"","Silence settled over the room.","Noah slowly nodded. ’Another dragon...’","His thoughts immediately wandered back to the labyrinth. The enormous stone doors. The ancient carvings. The black-scaled dragon with crimson eyes engraved upon them.","’Could they be connected...?’","If they were then the labyrinth wasn’t simply a normal labyrinth. It was hiding something far greater.","Noah lowered his head, completely absorbed in thought. Across from him... Akari quietly gazed out toward the peaceful garden.","She didn’t interrupt him. After spending sixty years alone. Silence had become something she was more than comfortable with.","The room remained quiet. Only the wind stirred the leaves outside.","Then another thought suddenly surfaced in Noah’s mind.","His eyes slowly narrowed.","’Wait... Something isn’t right.’","He began recalling the original game’s storyline.","’Damien... The protagonist was supposed to enter that labyrinth alone if my guess is right. Not me.’","His heartbeat quickened.","’Then...This place... Was never meant for me, Noah Eldritch.’","His thoughts raced even faster.","’Ophelia wasn’t one of the main heroines. She was only a supporting character. But...The game did have routes where additional heroines could join Damien later in the story.’","Noah’s pupils suddenly contracted.","’A hidden route...? A secret event...?’","He abruptly looked toward Akari.","Then everything seemed to connect.","’This was it... This was the storyline. Damien would have been the one pulled into this place. He would have met Akari. He would have helped her complete her dragon bloodline or whatever it is... Or perhaps find a way to escape. Then Akari would return to the outside world... Reunite with Ophelia... And naturally Ophelia’s feelings toward Damien would deepen because he had saved the mother she believed was dead.’","Noah slowly leaned back.","\"...No way.\"","The more he thought about it. The more plausible it became. Because he had unknowingly taken Damien’s place.","A wry smile appeared on his face.","’I’ve derailed another major event in the original plot. At this rate. The game’s story isn’t just changing. It’s becoming something completely different. But again... I never had any information about storyline. So it doesn’t matter.’","Noah remained silent for long.","Countless thoughts raced through Noah’s mind. The more he connected the pieces.","The clearer everything became.","’The labyrinth, it wasn’t created at random.’","It had been built specifically for Damien. Every challenge. Every trial. Every hidden mechanism. Everything had been carefully arranged so that, one day, the protagonist would reach this very place.","And the dragon the mysterious being that had imprisoned Akari here. It must have been the mastermind behind it all. Its intention had likely been simple.","To guide Damien here naturally. To have him meet Akari. To help her awaken her dragon bloodline completely before eventually returning to the outside world.","But that entire chain of events had been interrupted. By him. Noah Eldritch. He had unknowingly taken the protagonist’s place.","\"...\"","He let out a long sigh. It no longer mattered. The only thing that mattered now. Was finding a way back home.","His thoughts drifted away from the labyrinth as he turned his head toward the woman sitting beside him.","Akari remained seated gracefully in seiza, quietly enjoying the peaceful scenery beyond the veranda.","The morning sunlight gently illuminated her profile. Her raven-black hair, neatly tied into a bun, shimmered softly beneath the light.","The blue crystal hairpin reflected faint rays like a precious jewel. Despite the sapphire scales tracing the sides of her neck and reaching her right cheek.","She possessed an indescribable elegance. Almost otherworldly.","’At least...If I’m trapped somewhere. I’m trapped with a beautiful woman. Much better than spending my days with some grumpy old geezer.’","As though sensing his gaze. Akari slowly turned toward him. \"...Is there something on my face?\"","Her expression had already returned to its usual calm and indifferent state. She once again looked every bit like a strict and disciplined noblewoman.","Noah smiled warmly.","\"No. I was simply thinking.\"","He met her eyes.","\"Even after all these years...you’re still incredibly beautiful.\"","He paused before adding honestly,","\"I think you’re even more beautiful now than you were before you disappeared.\"","For a brief moment Akari simply stared at him. She didn’t blush. Nor did she avert her eyes like a young girl hearing her first compliment.","Instead she looked genuinely surprised. Almost confused. Her fingers slowly reached toward the blue scales on her neck. She gently brushed them.","\"You really think so?\"","There was a hint of uncertainty in her usually composed voice.","\"Even with these scales... You still think I’m beautiful?\"","Noah answered without the slightest hesitation.","\"Definitely.\"","He smiled.","\"They don’t make you look frightening. If anything... They make you look unique. Mysterious. They’re part of what makes you... you.\"","Of course he wisely kept the rest of his thoughts to himself.","’You’re far prettier than your daughter. And much easier to get along with. Let’s not say that out loud.’","Akari quietly observed him for several seconds. As though trying to determine whether he was merely being polite.","Eventually a soft chuckle escaped her lips.","\"I honestly don’t know how to respond.\" She lowered her hand from her neck. \"It’s been decades since someone last complimented my appearance.\"","There wasn’t any sadness in her voice. Only quiet nostalgia.","Noah laughed lightly. \"Then I suppose you’ll have to get used to it. Because I have a feeling I’ll be complimenting you quite often.\"","Akari looked at him. A gentle smile slowly bloomed across her face. \"I’ll look forward to that.\"","It was only a small smile. It was reserved and elegant.","Yet to someone who had lived in complete solitude for sixty years. It meant far more than Noah could imagine. She might not openly show it because of her personality.","But deep within her heart she felt happier than she had in decades. For the first time in sixty long years. This quiet house no longer felt empty.","The silence no longer felt lonely. She wasn’t alone anymore.","Noah suddenly glanced toward the scales on her neck again. Curiosity gradually replaced his previous thoughts.","\"By the way, Akari. May I touch them?\"","He pointed toward the sapphire-blue scales. \"I’ve never seen anything like them before. They look... surprisingly beautiful.\"","Akari looked at him for a moment. Then, without any hesitation. She gave a small nod. \"Of course. I don’t mind.\""]},{"number":255,"title":"Chapter 255: Akari [4]","paragraphs":["Noah moved a little closer and sat beside Akari.","His eyes were filled with curiosity as they carefully observed the sapphire-blue scales covering the sides of her neck. They were unlike anything he had ever seen.","Beautiful yet strangely intimidating. Slowly, he raised his right hand. His index and middle fingers gently reached toward the scales.","The moment they made contact.","\"Cold.\"","The word escaped his lips almost instinctively. The scales were much colder than he had expected. Not only that they were incredibly hard.","It felt as though he were touching polished steel.","Perhaps something even harder. His fingertips slowly traced along the smooth surface.","Each scale overlapped perfectly with the next, creating a mesmerizing pattern that reflected the morning light with a faint sapphire sheen.","He couldn’t help admiring them. \"They’re... really beautiful.\"","Noah had always been fascinated by dragons.","Like countless young men, he had grown up reading novels, watching anime, and imagining powerful dragons soaring through the skies.","And now a real dragon sat quietly beside him.","How could he not be fascinated?","Akari simply allowed him to continue. At first having someone touch her so closely felt a little strange. After all, no one had been this close to her in decades.","But when she noticed the genuine wonder in Noah’s eyes. The awkwardness slowly disappeared.","Instead she found his innocent curiosity rather endearing.","\"Do you really like them?\"","She asked softly, her blue slit-pupiled eyes resting on him.","Noah nodded immediately. \"Of course. They’re amazing. They’re cool.\"","He gently tapped one of the scales with his finger.","\"They’re incredibly solid.\"","Then another question came to mind.","\"How durable are they? If someone attacked your neck... Could an ordinary sword even cut through them?\"","Akari calmly shook her head.","\"No. A normal blade wouldn’t even leave a scratch.\"","She thought for a moment before adding,","\"Perhaps an S-Rank weapon might damage them. But anything below that...I highly doubt it.\"","Noah slowly nodded.","\"I see...\"","Without realizing it, he had leaned much closer. His attention remained fixed entirely on the dragon scales.","The warmth of his breath lightly brushed against the small section of normal skin near her throat that wasn’t covered by scales. The sensation tickled slightly.","Akari blinked once.","Yet she made no attempt to move away. Perhaps after sixty years of complete solitude. Having another human sitting this close no longer felt uncomfortable.","Instead it felt oddly comforting.","Noah suddenly looked up. \"Can I try something?\"","Akari tilted her head slightly. \"What do you want to try?\"","\"I want to test their durability.\" He pointed toward the scales. \"...By attacking them.\"","She blinked. \"You want to strike my neck?\"","He nodded earnestly. \"I won’t hold back. I want to know just how strong dragon scales really are.\"","Akari smiled faintly. \"So that’s what you’re curious about.\"","Without the slightest hesitation, she nodded.","\"Very well. Go ahead. Use your full strength. I’ll be fine.\"","Noah immediately stood up. As he did he suddenly realized he had been sitting extremely close. Because of their positions, Akari’s face was momentarily level with his waist.","He immediately took several steps backward before his imagination wandered somewhere inappropriate.","’Ahem... Let’s not think about that. No inappropriate thoughts.’","With a thought a steel sword emerged from his storage ring. Mana flowed rapidly from his core. A thin layer of icy mana wrapped around the blade, causing it to glow with a brilliant blue light.","He took a deep breath. \"I’m coming.\"","Akari remained seated in seiza without the slightest hint of concern.","\"Whenever you’re ready.\"","Noah pushed off the floor. His body shot forward. The sword traced a beautiful horizontal arc through the air. A crescent of pale-blue mana followed behind the blade.","CLANG!!","The impact echoed throughout the wooden house. A powerful vibration traveled through Noah’s arms.","His fingers went numb. It felt as though he had struck an indestructible wall forged from divine metal.","Meanwhile Akari hadn’t moved even an inch. Not even her posture changed.","Noah slowly lowered his sword before stepping back. He stared at her neck. There wasn’t even the tiniest scratch. Not a mark. Not a dent. There was nothing.","His eyes widened with amazement. \"That’s insane!\"","He couldn’t help laughing. \"These scales are incredible. I wish I had dragon scales covering my entire body.\"","Akari let out a soft chuckle. \"You certainly have an interesting sense of humor.\"","She lightly touched the scales herself. \"I don’t think having scales over your entire body would be very pleasant.\"","Noah shrugged. \"Maybe. But imagine if you could make them appear and disappear whenever you wanted. That would be amazing.\"","Akari nodded with a gentle smile. \"...That would be.\"","Silence returned. The peaceful atmosphere settled over the house once again.","Outside the birds continued singing. The breeze rustled through the trees.","Noah looked toward the endless forest. There was nothing for him to do.","There was no clues. No way home. No enemies to fight.","Only one option remained. He turned toward Akari.","\"Akari. I think I’ll spend my time training. There’s not much else I can do while I’m here.\"","He scratched his cheek with a helpless smile.","\"So...I was wondering. Would you be willing to teach me?\"","Akari looked at him quietly. Then she smiled. It was a warm smile. One that softened her usually calm and disciplined appearance.","\"Of course. I’d be happy to. It would actually be nice.\"","She looked out toward the garden.","\"I’ve spent sixty years here alone. Teaching someone...And simply having someone to talk. I think I’d enjoy that.\"","Noah’s expression softened. He couldn’t truly comprehend what sixty years of loneliness must have felt like.","She had no family here No friends. There was no one for conversation.","Yet she had endured it all without losing herself.","’How lonely must she have been?’","He silently looked at the woman beside him.","Then he made a quiet promise to himself.","’As long as I’m trapped here. I’ll spend as much time with her as I can. At the very least she won’t have to be alone anymore.’","There was no bad intention behind this decision. He really didn’t have any!! Believe in him!!","---","It was evening.","The golden light of the setting sun painted the forest in warm shades of orange and crimson.","A gentle breeze drifted through the trees, carrying the refreshing scent of flowers blooming near the lake.","Most of Noah’s day had been spent training.","Rather than practicing swordsmanship, he had devoted nearly the entire day to meditation.","His goal was simple.","To break through to the Condensed Core realm as quickly as possible.","Every hour mattered.","He still didn’t know how long he would remain trapped in this mysterious world.","Or what dangers awaited him after returning.","He slowly opened his eyes and exhaled.","A transparent blue screen appeared before him.","=== STATUS ===","Name: Noah Eldritch","Race: Human","Age: 19 Years","Strength: 368 [+41]","Speed: 364 [+34]","Stamina: 370 [+41]","Endurance: 359 [+38]","Charm: 651","Mana: 3543 [+420]","Core Rank: Awakened (High)","Potential: Mythical Core / Origin Core (???)","Profession: [Combatant Lv.2]","Technique: [Frozen Lotus Blade Art], [Flowing String Archery]","Affinity: Ice","Spells: [Ice Shard], [Frost Bind], [Snow Mist], [Ice Blizzard], [Crystal Bloom], [Winter Howl]","Innate Ability: [Ice Creation]","Passive Abilities: [Adaptive Learning], [Heart of Absolute Frost]","Active Ability: [Monarch’s Decree]","Bloodline: [Monarch of the Frost]","===================","A satisfied smile appeared on Noah’s face.","\"That’s better than I expected.\"","Although he hadn’t broken through yet. His mana had increased considerably. His physical attributes had also improved.","He estimated that, at his current pace. He would reach the Condensed Core realm within a month.","Perhaps even sooner if he found the right opportunity.","\"Are you checking your status?\"","Akari’s calm voice came from beside him.","She had been quietly watching over him throughout the day.","Most of his training consisted of meditation and mana circulation, so there wasn’t much she could actually teach.","Noah closed the status screen and nodded.","\"Yeah. My stats have improved quite a bit. I think I’ll reach the Condensed Core realm in less than a month.\"","Akari looked genuinely pleased.","\"That’s wonderful.\"","She smiled softly.","\"You’re remarkably talented for your age. Very few people your age are already standing this close to the Condensed Realm.\"","Noah scratched the back of his head with an awkward laugh.","\"Haha...I don’t think it’s that impressive. I was hoping to break through much sooner. But...\"","He shrugged.","\"I guess things don’t always go according to plan.\"","Akari gently shook her head.","\"Don’t rush yourself. A stable foundation is far more important than advancing quickly.\"","She looked toward the endless forest stretching beyond the lake.","\"Besides.You have plenty of time now.\"","Noah smiled wryly.","\"That’s true.\"","Unless he somehow found a way out. Time was the one thing he certainly wasn’t lacking.","Akari suddenly turned toward him.","\"How about taking a walk? The evening scenery is beautiful. I’d like to show you this place.\"","Noah looked around.","The warm sunlight filtering through the trees truly made the entire forest appear almost dreamlike.","There was no reason to refuse.","\"I’d like that.\"","He stood up with a smile. His clothes were damp with sweat after an entire day of training.","His hair clung slightly to his forehead.","\"I should probably wash up first. I don’t exactly want to smell like I’ve been training all day.\"","Akari covered her mouth with her sleeve as a faint laugh escaped her.","\"I think that’s a good idea. I’ll prepare dinner while you’re bathing.\"","Noah blinked. \"You don’t have to... wait dinner? How? Are there any vegetables here in forest?\"","She shook her head. \"Not exactly like our world. But there are few lesves and veggies which are edible. Though I don’t have any seasoning or salt.\"","\"Okay. And I don’t mind it. \"","Her gentle smile returned. \"I am kind of excited. I finally have someone to cook for.\"","For a brief moment.Neither of them spoke.","Then Noah smiled warmly. \"Thank you.\"","Without another word, he headed toward the small wooden bathhouse, while Akari quietly made her way toward the kitchen.","The lonely house no longer felt silent. It finally felt like a home.","---","[A/N: Hello, guys!! I’ve uploaded Akari’s image to the character profile on the novel’s page. You can go check it out and give her some popularity in the rankings!","Also, the image shows her without the scales on her neck and cheek.]"]},{"number":256,"title":"Chapter 256: Akari [5]","paragraphs":["How many years had it been since she had last seen another human?","Sixty long years had passed since she had been brought to this mysterious land for reasons she still didn’t understand.","Or perhaps ’taken’ would have been a more accurate word.","She had never come here willingly. She had been trapped. For sixty years. At first, she refused to accept her fate. There had to be another way out. There simply had to be.","So she searched. Alone in the vast wilderness, she wandered through forests, crossed rivers, climbed mountains, and explored every corner of this strange land.","She investigated every suspicious cave. Every broken ruin. Anything that looked remotely connected to the outside world.","But she found nothing. The monsters roaming this land were dangerous, but they posed little threat to her. Even back then, she had been powerful enough to defeat them.","So she continued searching. She never gave up. Days became weeks. Weeks became months. Months slowly turned into years.","Eventually reality crushed the last of her hope. There was no hidden exit. No forgotten portal. No secret path leading home. The only way she could see was the one the mysterious dragon had spoken of.","To awaken her dragon bloodline completely, to become a real dragon. Only then would she be allowed to leave.","So she devoted herself to training. When she had first arrived, she had already been an Aeternum Core Mid level.","During the first two years, while exploring this vast world and constantly battling monsters, she managed to break through into the Astral Core Low realm.","After reaching that level progress became painfully slow. Every breakthrough demanded years of effort.","So she meditated. Day after day. Year after year.","Fortunately this mysterious world possessed one incredible advantage. The density of mana here was nearly twice that of the outside world. It was an ideal environment for cultivation.","And so her new life began. A life defined by nothing but training. As the years passed, she eventually realized she couldn’t continue sleeping beneath trees or inside caves forever.","So she gathered timber. Cut countless trees. Collected stone and other materials. Little by little she built herself a home. She couldn’t help smiling whenever she remembered those early days.","She had known nothing about carpentry. Yet after decades of trial and error. She had unknowingly become quite skilled at it.","Every piece of furniture. She had built with her own hands. Time continued flowing.","Every single day. She missed her daughter. The little girl who had only been seven years old when they were separated.","Fortunately she still possessed a few photographs inside her storage ring. Whenever the loneliness became unbearable.","She would quietly take them out. Sit beside the lake. And look at Ophelia’s smiling face for hours. Those photographs became her greatest treasure.","Loneliness was far crueler than any monster she had ever fought.","To distract herself she trained. When she grew tired of training. She learned new skills.","She tried to cook something from unknown fruits or veggies. Woodworking and gardening. Anything that could occupy her mind.","Even so nothing could fill the emptiness inside her heart. There were nights when the silence became almost unbearable.","No voices, laughter, conversations and only herself. Slowly she began talking to the animals living nearby.","She protected them from monsters. Fed injured creatures. Created a safe haven around her home where they could live peacefully.","The deer grew accustomed to her. The rabbits no longer fled. Even birds would occasionally perch upon her shoulder.","Yet no matter how many animals surrounded her. They could never replace another human being.","Years passed. Then decades.","Eventually she grew accustomed to solitude. Living alone no longer felt painful. The days seemed shorter. The silence became familiar.","It had become her normal. After living the same lonely life for sixty years. She believed nothing would ever change. Then everything changed.","\"...Uhm...\"","A young man’s awkward voice echoed through her home.","She slowly turned. Standing at one of the room of her house was a young man with fair skin and snow-white hair. He scratched the back of his head awkwardly before giving her a polite smile.","\"...Hello?\"","Akari froze. Her mind completely stopped working.","’...What...?’","She simply stood there motionless like a statue. Was she hallucinating? No, even during the darkest nights, when she had cried alone until exhaustion, she had never imagined something this vividly.","She blinked multiple times. The figure remained.","\"...Hello, ma’am?\"","The young man spoke again. His voice finally pulled her back to reality. The moment she truly heard him. Her blue eyes widened.","\"...A...\"","Her lips parted.","\"...Human?\"","The word escaped almost as a whisper. Her voice carried unmistakable disbelief.","The young man blinked in confusion. \"Well...\"","He smiled awkwardly. \"I am human.\"","The instant those words reached her ears. Every ounce of composure she had maintained for sixty years shattered.","’He’s really here...? A human...? Standing... in front of me...? No... I have to make sure...’","Before he could say another word she disappeared. Not by teleportation. Simply by moving faster than his eyes could follow.","She reappeared directly before him. Both of her hands gently cupped his cheeks.","It felt warm, so unbelievably warm.","For sixty years these hands had touched nothing but trees, animals and monsters she had slain.","Tools she had crafted. Now they were touching another human being. His skin was soft. His warmth spread into her palms. It felt so real. Almost too real.","Still she had to be certain. She gently tilted his face upward. Then downward. Then to the left. Then to the right.","Examining him from every possible angle. As though verifying the existence of the greatest miracle she had ever witnessed.","’He’s real...He’s really here!’","Her heart trembled. She wanted to cry. She wanted to hug him tightly. She wanted to ask countless questions. She wanted to hear another person’s voice for hours without stopping.","Yet sixty years of isolation had changed her. Her emotions no longer surfaced naturally. It felt as though they had been buried beneath decades of silence. Or suppressed by herself.","She struggled to express what she truly felt. Only a tiny fraction escaped.","\"...A human...\"","Her voice quivered.","\"...A real human.\"","There was joy, disbelief, excitement in her voice. Every emotion she had suppressed for sixty years mixed together in that single sentence.","And that was how Akari Narukami met Noah Eldritch.","The first human she had seen in sixty long years."]},{"number":257,"title":"Chapter 257: Akari [6]","paragraphs":["A little while later.","Akari returned from the kitchen carrying a large wooden pot. Steam rose gently from it, filling the room with a pleasant herbal aroma.","Noah was already seated at a low wooden table in the traditional style common throughout the Eastern Duchies. Its design reminded him very much of the tables described in old Japanese culture.","After taking a bath, he had changed into a fresh set of spare clothes from his storage ring. His body finally felt clean after an entire day of training.","Akari carefully placed the pot on the table.","\"Dinner is ready.\"","Noah looked curiously at the steaming pot before glancing around the room.","Then something occurred to him.","\"Wait.\"","He looked back at her.","\"How did you cook all this using only wooden utensils?\"","Akari smiled faintly.","\"I don’t.\"","She pointed toward a corner of the kitchen.","\"There are several smooth stones stacked together there. I built a simple stone stove years ago. I gather dry firewood from the forest and use a flint stone to start a fire.\"","She continued calmly,","\"The wooden pot never touches the flames directly. I suspend it above the fire using a wooden frame reinforced with thick green vines. It takes a little longer than metal cookware, but these trees produce wood that resists heat surprisingly well.\"","Noah looked genuinely impressed.","\"That’s amazing.\"","He glanced back at the pot.","\"So... what did you make?\"","Akari thought for a moment.","\"Soup. I made it from several edible green leaves that grow nearby. I don’t know their proper names. I also added a few fruits that naturally have a salty flavor instead of using salt. And some small spicy berries to give it a little warmth.\"","She looked slightly embarrassed.","\"It’s... rather simple. I hope you don’t mind. No way. It already smells incredible.\"","Akari quietly brought two wooden bowls before carefully ladling the soup into them. She handed one bowl and a carved wooden spoon to Noah.","He accepted it with a smile. \"Thank you.\"","The soup was still steaming. He gently blew across the surface before taking his first spoonful. The warm broth spread across his tongue.","His eyes widened. He froze.","Across the table Akari quietly watched every tiny change in his expression.","’I hope he likes it...’","She had never cared much about flavor. Living alone for sixty years meant food had simply become fuel. She honestly had no idea whether her cooking would suit someone else’s taste.","Seeing Noah remain completely silent only made her more nervous.","’Did I fail? Maybe I’m actually terrible at cooking. What was the point of spending all those years learning if it still tastes awful...?’","Noah slowly lowered the spoon. Then looked directly at her. He kept staring.","Akari’s brows slowly furrowed.","\"You didn’t like it?\"","She quietly asked. A trace of disappointment surfaced in her eyes.","’So I really am a terrible cook. All those years. Completely useless.’","\"Akari...\"","He suddenly spoke.","\"Will you marry me?\"","\"Huh?\"","She blinked. Her mind completely stopped.","’Did he just said...Marry Me?’","Her eyes instantly widened.","\"W-What?!\" She almost stood up in surprise. \"What are you saying all of a sudden? Yo- You...I-I am married... No...\"","She quickly corrected herself.","\"I’m not anymore...But... I’m so much older than you! How can you suddenly propose to me? We only met today!\"","Without realizing it a faint blush slowly spread across her cheeks. Her carefully maintained composure crumbled completely. It was from embarrassment. Since he younger age no one ever dares to propose her. It was her first time, that also for marriage","Noah stared at her for a second before bursting into laughter. \"Hahaha! Akari! Calm down. At least let me finish.\"","He waved both hands helplessly. \"I wasn’t seriously proposing. I meant your cooking is so unbelievably delicious that it makes me want to marry the person who cooked it. It’s just a saying. My way of telling you how much I love your cooking.\"","\"...\"","Akari remained frozen. Then relief slowly washed over her.","’So that’s what he meant.’","For one terrifying moment. She had genuinely believed he was proposing.","Noah continued eating happily.","\"You know...You looked incredibly adorable just now. And honestly... I don’t think age really matters. I’m sure plenty of men would still want to marry someone as beautiful as you.\"","\"...\"","’This boy!’","He said it so naturally. Without hesitation or any embarrassment. It genuinely sounded as though he believed every word.","Akari slowly took a deep breath. She forced herself to regain her usual calm expression.","\"Thank you.\"","She answered in her familiar composed voice.","\"I’m... glad to hear that.\"","Noah chuckled before extending his now-empty bowl toward her.","\"Another serving, please. And you should eat too. It’ll get cold.\"","She quietly accepted the bowl.","\"Alright.\"","She gently poured him another serving.","As she did, Noah rested his chin on one hand and casually spoke,","\"To be honest... We’re the only two people here. We have no idea how long we’ll remain trapped. It could be months or even years.\"","She paused halfway through pouring.","\"Go on.\"","He smiled mischievously.","\"So maybe... We should just get married while we’re here.\"","\"...\"","\"...\"","\"Noah!!\"","She finally exploded.","\"That is incredibly improper! You don’t say things like that to an older woman!\"","Her face flushed bright red.","’This young man...He’s openly... what they say? what was that word? hah yes! flirting! He is flirting with me! Without even trying to hide it!’","And somehow an absurd thought briefly crossed her mind.","’If...if we really stayed here together. We might have to stay for few more years.. i don’t know how many... so being close to him that way.. just two of us..’","She immediately shook her head.","’No! What am I thinking?!’","It wasn’t that she had suddenly developed feelings for him. Far from it. But after sixty years of complete solitude. Simply imagining sharing countless years with another person felt strangely comforting.","She looked at him with narrowed eyes. \"I don’t even look normal anymore.\"","She lightly touched the scales along her neck.","\"And I’m over ninety years old. If I actually looked like a ninety-year-old grandmother... Would you still say the same thing?\"","She handed his bowl back to him.","Noah accepted it before thoughtfully looking up.","Then he smirked.","\"If you really looked ninety... And your life was almost over...Then probably not.\"","Akari nodded once. \"See?\"","\"But...\" He continued. \"If you still had hundreds of years left to live. Even if you looked like an old grandmother. I’d probably still—\"","\"You are absolutely shameless.\"","Akari interrupted with her eyes closed. Her voice had become perfectly calm again. Almost frighteningly calm. Her hands clenched tightly atop her kimono.","She slowly opened her eyes. \"...Is this truly how young men treat women nowadays?\"","Before she could continue.","\"Hahaha! Alright! I’m sorry!\"","Noah quickly raised both hands in surrender.","\"I’ll stop teasing you. I promise. I was just having a little fun.\"","Akari stared at him silently for several seconds.","Eventually she sighed.","Then without realizing it herself. A small smile formed on her lips.","’This feeling...Sharing a meal... Talking...Laughing together. It’s far warmer than I remembered.’","She searched her memories. She honestly couldn’t remember the last time she had enjoyed a dinner like this.","Not even with Lionel. Not even when Ophelia was still a child. As a noble and traditional lady, most of her dinners were normal and filled with disciplined. And those memories had long since faded beneath sixty years of loneliness.","She slowly shook her head before looking at Noah again. \"You’re too much.\"","Noah grinned. \"You’ll get used to me.\"","Akari smiled back.","\"Perhaps. I will.\" She finally picked up her own bowl. For the first time in decades she wasn’t eating alone.","That simple meal shared across a small wooden table. Filled with harmless teasing, quiet laughter, and ordinary conversation. Became the warmest dinner she had ever experienced in her entire life."]},{"number":258,"title":"Chapter 258: She’s Dangerous","paragraphs":["Crunch.","Crunch.","Stomp.","Soft footsteps echoed through the silent forest beneath the night sky.","Noah and Akari walked side by side along a narrow path winding between towering ancient trees.","Although there was no moon visible overhead, the forest was strangely illuminated by a gentle silver glow. The mysterious moonlight filtered through the thick canopy, casting shimmering patterns across the ground.","A cool breeze drifted through the woods, gently rustling the leaves overhead. For a long moment, neither of them spoke.","The peaceful silence was oddly comforting.","Noah took a slow breath, enjoying the fresh air.","\"It’s actually not that bad here,\" he said with a faint smile.","\"Everything is so quiet... so peaceful. The gentle wind, the forest... it’s relaxing.\"","Akari looked around before smiling softly. \"Yes...\"","She brushed a loose strand of hair behind her ear.","\"If you have someone to share it with... this place isn’t such a terrible place to live.\"","Noah smiled. \"Well, now you have me.\"","He folded his hands behind his head as they continued walking.","\"So from now on, you won’t have to spend your days here alone anymore.\"","A warmth flickered across Akari’s eyes. \"...You’re right.\"","Her voice was quieter than before. \"I suppose this place has become much more enjoyable.\"","The two continued walking in comfortable silence. After a while, Noah suddenly remembered something.","\"Oh, right. I noticed something this afternoon while I was meditating.\"","He looked toward her. \"The mana density here is incredible. It feels much richer than the outside world.\"","Akari nodded. \"That’s correct. The concentration of mana here is nearly twice that of the outside world. It allows us to progress much faster.\"","Noah’s eyes brightened. \"No wonder...\"","He had already noticed how quickly his mana recovered after training. Now it finally made sense.","\"Actually...\"","He turned toward her curiously.","\"What rank are you now?\"","Akari glanced at him before answering with a calm smile.","\"I’ve reached the Sovereign Core—High Stage.\"","Noah’s footsteps abruptly stopped.","\"W-What?\"","He stared at her in complete disbelief. \"You’ve actually reached the peak of the human realm?\"","’She is as strong as Principal Adrian...more maybe more.’ He thought.","Akari covered her mouth with one hand and chuckled elegantly. \"Hehe... Yes. I’ve had sixty years with nothing to do except train. It would have been stranger if I hadn’t reached this level.\"","Noah let out a long breath. \"That’s... That’s incredible.\"","Then another thought crossed his mind. \"So... Your natural potential limit was Sovereign Core?\"","Akari’s smile became slightly more subdued. \"...Yes. It was.\"","Noah looked at her with renewed admiration. ’She’s unbelievably powerful. A Sovereign Core. She’s probably among the strongest humans alive. If anyone can help me grow stronger... it’s definitely her.’","A determined smile appeared on his face. ’I should learn everything I can from her.’","Akari resumed walking.","Realizing he had stopped, Noah hurried to catch up. For a brief, unguarded moment his gaze drifted to her figure.","Even beneath the elegant blue-and-black kimono, her silhouette was impossible to ignore—tall, composed, and quietly commanding.","The traditional obi cinched her slender waist with deliberate grace, while the soft, flowing fabric traced the long line of her back and the full, womanly curve of her hips.","The heavy folds could not quite conceal the rounded weight of her rear, the subtle sway of it with each measured step.","’She really is a milf,’ he thought, the observation landing with a quiet, heated certainty.","Noah immediately looked away and quietly cleared his throat.","’Get yourself together. She’s kind enough to take me in and help me. Don’t start thinking nonsense.’","He shook his head with a helpless smile before matching her pace once more.","Soon, the two disappeared deeper into the peaceful forest, their quiet conversation blending with the gentle whisper of the night breeze.","After walking for a while, they arrived at the tranquil lake where Noah had first awakened.","Moonlight shimmered softly across the crystal-clear water, painting silver ripples over its surface. A gentle breeze drifted across the lake, carrying the scent of fresh grass and wildflowers.","Noah stopped near the shore.","\"This is where I first woke up.\"","Akari followed his gaze.","\"So this is where you brought by that portal...\"","There was a strange softness in her voice.","She quietly lowered herself onto the grass, sitting gracefully in seiza, her legs folded neatly beneath her kimono. Even such a simple movement carried an effortless elegance.","Noah sat down beside her.","He sat close enough to enjoy her company. Yet careful enough to keep a respectful distance.","For a while, neither of them spoke. They simply watched the peaceful lake together.","The silence between them wasn’t awkward. It was comforting. After a while, Noah smiled. \"Akari.\"","\"Hm?\"","\"When can I finally see your full dragon form?\"","There was unmistakable excitement in his voice.","Akari glanced sideways before letting out a soft laugh.","\"So eager?\"","\"I am very much eager. Every man wanted to see a real dragon ever since they were child.\"","She smiled gently.","\"Then tomorrow. I’ll show you. And while we’re at it... I’ll help with your training as well.\"","Noah’s eyes lit up.","\"Really?\"","She nodded.","\"Of course.\"","A comfortable silence settled over them once again.","Noah looked at the beautiful woman sitting beside him.","Her fair skin glowed beneath the moonlight. The sapphire-blue scales along her neck shimmered like polished gemstones.","Her elegant profile looked almost unreal.","’She’s... beautiful. Not merely because of her appearance. There was a grace about her. A maturity born from decades of solitude.’","Something that made her seem both gentle and heartbreakingly lonely.","Noah lowered his eyes.","Her chest was a huge pair. Noah knew that much. Even tightly bound by her kimono, they still looked big. In reality, they were probably enormous.","Again he shook his head.","’Damn, this woman is dangerous for my heart. First Lyria and Arisha. Now her. Sometimes I wished I was like those protagonists who never react to beautiful ladies—always cold and detached like some gay. Sigh... I don’t want to be gay... I’m still better than them.’","In the end, Noah accepted his inner demon and slid closer to her until their thighs were only inches from touching.","’Should I tell her? About Ophelia. About everything that happened.’","His chest tightened. He couldn’t. He was still worried how she would react.","Not yet, not on the very first day."]},{"number":259,"title":"Chapter 259: Daily Life With Akari [1]","paragraphs":["He wasn’t ready to tell a mother that the daughter she cherished had become someone he could barely stand to face.","\"Akari.\"","She turned toward him.","\"Yes? There are... a few things I haven’t told you.\"","She looked at him quietly.","Noah forced a smile. \"I’m... not sure how to say them.\"","Akari’s expression softened. \"Then don’t.\"","He blinked. \"When you feel ready...You can tell me. There is no need to force yourself.\"","Her voice was calm. There was patience. Without a trace of pressure.","Noah slowly nodded. \"...Thank you.\"","Silence returned. The only sounds were the gentle movement of the lake...","The whispering leaves and the distant chorus of insects beneath the mysterious moonlight.","Noah stared quietly at the water.","’What should I do...? I don’t know what to talk about... We’re close... Will she lean on me and rest her head on my shoulder...? No, she’d never do something like that. Maybe... I could try...’ He thought.","And without realizing it his body slowly leaned toward her.","His shoulder brushed lightly against hers. Then, almost instinctively. He rested his head gently against her shoulder.","Akari flinched ever so slightly. \"...Noah? What are you doing?\"","He let out a tired laugh.","\"...Honestly...I don’t know.\"","He closed his eyes.","\"I just...felt like doing this.\"","A weary smile appeared on his lips.","\"I’m exhausted. So much has happened these past few days. I don’t even remember the last time I truly relaxed.\"","Akari remained perfectly still. She could have moved away.","She didn’t. Instead she simply let him stay there. His warmth spread through the sleeve of her kimono.","It felt strangely comforting.","For the first time in sixty years someone was leaning on her. Trusting her and depending on her.","She slowly lowered her gaze toward him. His snowy-white hair swayed gently with the breeze.","Without thinking she raised one hand. Her fingers gently brushed through his soft hair.","They moved lowly and tenderly. It was as if someone simply trying to reassure another lonely soul.","\"You are safe here...\"","Her voice was barely above a whisper.","\"So don’t worry anymore.\"","Noah’s body gradually relaxed beneath her gentle touch.","The embarrassment he had felt only moments ago quietly disappeared. His breathing became slower.","His eyelids grew heavier with every gentle stroke of her fingers.","Before he realized it he had fallen asleep.","Akari looked down at the sleeping young man resting peacefully against her shoulder.","A faint smile appeared on her lips.","\"...You really fell asleep.\"","She whispered softly. There was no annoyance in her voice. There was only warmth.","She continued stroking his hair for a while longer.","Then very gently she rested her own cheek against the top of his head. Closing her eyes, she listened to the quiet rhythm of his breathing.","\"...It’s wonderful...\"","She murmured.","\"...having someone beside you.\"","The loneliness that had accompanied her for sixty long years. Didn’t seem nearly as heavy anymore.","Under the quiet moonlight. Beside the peaceful lake... The two remained together in silence.","Neither of them spoke another word.","Yet somehow it was the warmest night Akari had experienced since the day she had been trapped in this forgotten world.","---","Morning arrived before Noah even realized it. The peaceful night seemed to pass in the blink of an eye.","Noah, he had slept without fear. There was no worry.","Inside one of the wooden rooms, a simple bed had been made from countless soft leaves gathered together. A single enormous leaf, nearly the size of a person, had been laid over it like a blanket.","Noah lay comfortably upon it.","\"...Mmm.\" His eyelids twitched. Indicating he was waking up slowly.","Slowly, he opened his eyes. \"Yawn...\"","He stretched lazily before blinking at the familiar wooden ceiling above him.","\"I’m inside the house.\"","The memories of the previous night gradually returned.","\"The lake... Akari... I must’ve fallen asleep.\"","He rubbed his eyes. \"Did she carry me back here after I fell asleep?\"","He turned his head to look around.","\"...Where is she?\"","Then his breathing stopped. His blue eyes widened.","Lying beside him separated by barely the width of a single hand was Akari.","She was sleeping on her side, facing him.","Her long raven-black hair had loosened slightly during the night, a few silky strands resting gently across her cheek.","Her breathing was slow and steady.","The morning sunlight filtering through the window softly illuminated her peaceful face.","Without her usual composed expression. She looked surprisingly gentle.","Almost vulnerable.","Noah blinked several times.","’Wait a minute...D–did we sleep beside each other all night?’","His mind went completely blank.","’This can’t be real.’ He couldn’t believe on such things easily.","Unable to believe what he was seeing, he quietly pinched his own cheek.","\"Ow...\"","The slight sting made him wince.","’It’s real. It’s not a dream. Damnation!!’","He slowly looked back at Akari.","She still hadn’t awakened. She simply continued sleeping peacefully, completely defenseless.","A faint smile unknowingly appeared on Noah’s lips.","’She looks cute. Despite being over so many years. It’s honestly unfair. I wil have very hard time. How can someone who’s lived for so many decades still look this graceful?’","He quietly chuckled to himself. Looking at her calm sleeping face. An irresistible impulse suddenly surfaced.","’Should I pinch her cheek?’","His fingers even twitched slightly. But after a moment.","He sighed.","’No. I’d probably get punched through the wall.’","The thought alone made him abandon the idea.","Instead he simply lay there quietly.Watching her peaceful sleeping face.","Listening to the soft rhythm of her breathing.","Time seemed to slow. Then Akari’s eyelashes fluttered.","Her eyelids trembled gently.","Slowly those beautiful sapphire-blue eyes opened.","Their gazes met.","For a brief moment neither of them spoke.","Her lips curved into a small smile. \"Good morning.\"","For Noah, this might have been the best morning he had ever experienced in his entire life.","---","[A/N: Guy’s... She’s going to be a female lead.Lyria, Arisha, Sefira, Morgana and Akari. Total five female leads so far. Though he is still a single hehe~]"]},{"number":260,"title":"Chapter 260: Daily Life With Akari [2]","paragraphs":["\"WHOOOOOO!!\"","Noah’s excited shout echoed across the endless forest.","His snow-white hair whipped wildly in the rushing wind as an enormous grin spread across his face.","His blue eyes sparkled with pure excitement. The reason was simple. For the first time in his life he was riding a real dragon.","High above the endless sea of emerald trees, a colossal dragon soared through the sky.","Its wings stretched nearly fifty meters from tip to tip, each powerful beat sending violent gusts sweeping across the forest below. Every movement carried overwhelming grace, as though the creature itself commanded the heavens.","Dark sapphire-blue scales covered its entire body. They weren’t simply blue.","Under the morning sunlight, each scale shimmered with shades of midnight, cobalt, and violet, reflecting the light like countless polished gemstones. Whenever the dragon tilted its body, the scales gleamed beautifully, resembling an ocean beneath a storm.","Its elegant neck curved proudly through the sky.","Two magnificent horns arched backward from its head, smooth and dark as polished obsidian, faint streaks of blue lightning dancing between them every few seconds.","Its eyes, they were enormous.","Brilliant sapphire eyes with narrow vertical pupils, calm yet majestic enough to make anyone instinctively lower their gaze.","Behind it, a powerful tail stretched gracefully through the air, nearly half the creature’s total length. Every gentle swing helped guide its flight with effortless precision.","Around its body tiny arcs of blue lightning occasionally flickered between its scales before disappearing into the rushing wind.","The dragon itself radiated an overwhelming aura.","She was majestic. She looked ancient. And very beautiful.","A true ruler of storms. It was none other than Akari. In her complete dragon form.","Thirty-five meters from the tip of her snout to the end of her tail.","Noah sat securely near the base of her neck, gripping one of her sturdy scales for balance.","The wind roared around him.","Below the forest looked no larger than patches of green moss. Rivers shimmered like silver threads weaving across the landscape.","The breathtaking scenery stole his breath away.","Akari’s deep, resonant voice reached him over the wind.","\"Are you enjoying yourself?\"","Even in her dragon form, her voice retained its familiar gentleness.","Noah laughed loudly.","\"Enjoying? This is amazing! I’ve dreamed to ride a dragon! I never thought I’d actually get to ride a dragon!\"","Akari let out a soft rumbling laugh.","\"I’m glad.\"","The giant dragon banked gently, gliding above another stretch of forest.","\"So where are we going?\" Noah shouted over the rushing wind.","\"I’m taking you somewhere suitable for today’s training.\"","\"Oh?\"","His curiosity immediately piqued.","\"What kind of place?\"","\"You’ll see soon.\"","Several minutes later Akari began descending. Her massive wings spread even wider.","With every beat, hurricane-like gusts swept across the treetops below.","Branches bent violently. Leaves spiraled into the air. Small animals scattered in every direction.","The sheer pressure generated by her landing was enough to shake the surrounding forest.","Boom.","Her enormous body landed gracefully in a wide clearing. Despite her incredible size, the impact was surprisingly controlled.","Noah jumped from her body and landed on grass.","She folded her wings against her body. A gentle sapphire light slowly enveloped her. The gigantic dragon began shrinking. Her scales dissolved into streams of shimmering blue mana.","Her wings faded. Her horns disappeared. Within moments standing where the dragon had been was Akari once again.","She wore the same elegant blue-and-black kimono as before. Not even a single strand of her hair appeared out of place.","Noah blinked several times. \"...That’s unbelievable.\"","He couldn’t help staring.","’Every time she transforms, her clothes disappear... Then reappear perfectly once she’s human again. Dragon transformation is seriously unfair. A morph ability I guess.’","He almost wanted that ability for himself.","Akari noticed his curious expression and smiled knowingly.","\"What is it?\"","\"No...\"","He scratched his cheek awkwardly.","\"I was just amazed by your transformation. It looks incredible.\"","A faint smile appeared on her lips.","\"Thank you.\"","She then turned toward the entrance of a dense section of the forest.","Her expression became slightly more serious.","\"Today’s training begins here.\"","Noah immediately straightened. \"What will I be doing?\"","Akari pointed deeper into the forest.","\"Run.\"","\"...Run?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Inside this forest live mostly plant-type monsters. There are also a few ordinary low-ranked monsters.\"","She looked directly into his eyes.","\"Your objective is simple. Enter from this side. Then survive. And reach the opposite side of the forest.\"","Noah smiled confidently. \"That doesn’t sound too difficult.\"","Akari raised one finger. \"There are conditions.\"","His smile slowly faded. \"...I knew there’d be a catch.\"","She nodded. \"You are forbidden from attacking. No magic. No weapons. No offensive abilities. You may only use mana to strengthen your body and improve your movement.Nothing else.\"","Noah blinked. \"That actually sounds difficult.\"","\"It is.\" Akari nodded.","\"The purpose isn’t to defeat enemies. It’s to sharpen your survival instincts. Learn to read danger. Learn to evade. Learn when to move. Learn how to sneak away when face strong monsters. And most importantly...\"","She smiled reassuringly.","\"I’ll be watching. If your life is ever truly in danger. I’ll save you. So don’t worry.\"","Noah grinned.","\"Understood.\"","He gave her an exaggerated salute.","\"Yes, Master!\"","Akari couldn’t help smiling at his enthusiasm.","\"Good.\"","She folded her arms. \"Now...Tell me. Are you ready?\"","\"Yes.\" Noah took a deep breath. \"I’m ready.\"","Akari gave a satisfied nod. \"Good. Then go.\"","Without another word, Noah pushed off the ground.","Whoosh!","His body shot toward the dense forest. Within moments, the open clearing disappeared behind him.","Ancient trees surrounded him from every direction.","Towering trunks stretched high into the sky, their branches weaving together into a thick canopy that blocked much of the sunlight. Shafts of golden light pierced through occasional gaps, creating shifting patterns across the forest floor.","Crunch.","Crunch.","His footsteps echoed softly as he ran across fallen leaves and tangled roots. His breathing remained steady.","’Nothing yet...’","He cautiously observed his surroundings while maintaining a moderate pace. Every sense remained alert. The forest was unnaturally quiet.","There were no birds. There were no insects. Only the sound of his own footsteps.","Mana flowed from his core. A pale blue aura wrapped around his legs, strengthening every muscle. His speed steadily increased.","Whoosh!","He weaved between trees with practiced movements. Then his eyes narrowed.","Up ahead several enormous flowers stood silently among the trees. Each one towered over him, nearly twice his height.","Their thick green stalks resembled tree trunks.","Large crimson petals surrounded a circular center lined with dozens of folded spikes that looked disturbingly similar to teeth.","Their roots remained buried in the earth.","They couldn’t walk at first glance. They looked like ordinary giant flowers.","Noah slowed slightly. He knew they were not normal since he had faced them before.","’Plant-type monsters...Just like Akari mentioned. Also, I had encountered similar monsters on first day.’"]},{"number":261,"title":"Chapter 261: Daily Life With Akari [3]","paragraphs":["He carefully adjusted his path to pass between two of them. The instant he entered their range.","Rustle!","Every flower suddenly moved. The petals unfolded completely. Rows upon rows of jagged teeth emerged from within the blossoms.","The entire flower twisted toward Noah. Their enormous mouths opened wide.","SKREEEE!!","An ear-piercing shriek echoed through the forest.","’They noticed me!’","Without hesitation, Noah accelerated.","Boom!","One gigantic flower lunged toward him. Although rooted to the ground, its flexible stalk bent with terrifying speed.","Its massive head shot forward like a striking snake.","Noah instinctively threw himself sideways. The monstrous flower slammed into the ground where he had been a fraction of a second earlier.","BOOM!","Soil exploded into the air. Wood splinters flew everywhere.","Noah rolled across the ground before immediately regaining his footing.","’Fast! Much faster than yesterday!’","Before he could recover.","Whip!","Thick vines burst from the bushes to his right. They lashed toward his legs like living whips.","Noah jumped. The vines narrowly missed his ankles.","The moment he landed another flower attacked from the opposite side. Its enormous mouth snapped shut with a deafening crunch.","CRACK!!","A tree trunk nearly half a meter thick shattered between its jaws. Cold sweat ran down Noah’s back.","’If that was my body... Damn! I need to run like I am running for my life.’","He didn’t dare finish the thought. Remembering Akari’s instructions, he resisted every urge to summon ice.","’No magic. No attacks. I just have to run.’","He clenched his teeth. Mana surged through his legs again.","Whoosh!","His speed exploded. He zigzagged through the forest with sharp changes of direction, using trees as cover whenever possible.","Another vine shot toward his chest. He twisted his torso at the last possible moment.","Swish!","The thorn-covered vine grazed his shoulder.","Rip!","His shirt tore open. A red line appeared across his skin.","Blood slowly trickled down his arm.","\"Tch... Just a scratch.\"","He didn’t slow down. Instead, he pushed even harder.","Behind him the flowers continued shrieking. Dozens of vines whipped wildly through the forest. Some pierced tree trunks. Others shattered rocks. The entire forest seemed alive.","Noah’s breathing gradually became heavier. His body darted between countless attacks.","He leaped. Then slide, then duck and roll.","Every movement came purely from instinct. Twice more, thorny vines managed to scrape his arms. One sharp thorn grazed his thigh, leaving another shallow cut.","The injuries weren’t serious. But they steadily accumulated.","More importantly his concentration couldn’t slip even once.","One mistake one moment of hesitation... And those monstrous flowers would swallow him whole.","Far behind him standing atop a thick tree branch...","Akari silently watched everything.","She made no attempt to interfere. Her sapphire eyes calmly followed every movement Noah made through the forest.","A faint smile slowly appeared on her lips.","\"Good...\"","She murmured softly.","\"Don’t think. Move. Trust your instincts. That’s the first lesson.\"","Below her Noah continued sprinting through the sea of monstrous flowers, desperately weaving between countless snapping jaws and razor-sharp vines while refusing to draw his sword or cast a single spell.","His real training had only just begun.","For next few months all he have to do was training.","---","While Noah was busy training in an unknown land...","The outside world had descended into chaos.","---","In a magnificent hall, a beautiful woman sat silently upon an elegant throne.","She wore a flowing white robe embroidered with delicate golden patterns.","Her long snow-white hair faded into brilliant crimson flame at the ends, resembling dancing flames. Her striking eyes carried the same fiery hue, giving her an almost divine presence.","It was Sefira.","She rested one elbow against the armrest, her chin supported by her hand.","Her gaze was distant.","She was completely lost in thought. The recent monster outbreaks across the Empire refused to leave her mind.","BEEP!","A soft notification echoed through the silent hall.","Sefira blinked before reaching into her robe and pulling out a small communication device.","It was a circular metallic artifact with a crystal screen embedded in its center.","She tapped the surface lightly.","The screen flickered to life. A familiar face appeared.","\"Have you learned anything, Victor?\" she asked immediately.","\"What exactly is happening?\"","\"I’ve already dealt with as many monsters as I could in the nearby towns and villages.\"","\"They’re appearing far too frequently.\"","Victor nodded from the other side.","\"Yes, my lady. I’ve gathered some important information. It came from Instructor Morgana. After receiving her report, the Principal immediately called a meeting with the senior instructors. I was present.\"","Sefira straightened in her seat.","\"Tell me everything.\"","Victor didn’t waste any time.","He carefully explained everything Morgana had reported.","By the time Victor finished. The calm expression on Sefira’s face had completely disappeared.","\"So...\"","She spoke slowly.","\"You’re telling me that Noah and Damien’s expedition into the labyrinth is connected to everything happening across the Empire?\"","\"Yes.\"","Victor nodded gravely. \"That’s our current conclusion.\"","Sefira’s brows knitted together.","\"And Noah he’s still missing?\"","Victor lowered his gaze.","\"Yes. Morgana believes there’s a strong possibility he was pulled into another pocket dimension connected to the labyrinth.\"","Silence filled the room.","Sefira slowly closed her eyes.","Her fingers tightened around the communication device.","\"I understand.\"","She opened her eyes once more.Their fiery glow had become much sharper.","\"You’ve done well, Victor. Continue gathering information. I’ll personally investigate this matter from here.\"","Victor bowed respectfully.","\"Yes, my lady.\"","The connection ended.","The crystal screen dimmed.","Sefira remained standing in silence for several moments.","A worried sigh escaped her lips.","\"Noah. Where have you gone this time?\"","She clenched her fist.","\"Dammit!\"","She was already feeling sad and guilty for fooling Noah. Showing death of his friend Mary.","Now he was missing.","\"Hope he is fine. I still have to apologize to him in future.\"","The memories she share with Noah came.","Without another word, she turned and walked toward the massive doors of the hall.","Her destination had already been decided.","Everhold City.","She intended to investigate the labyrinth herself.","If Noah had truly disappeared into another dimension. Then she would try her best to find him."]},{"number":262,"title":"Chapter 262: Daily Life With Akari [4]","paragraphs":["It was another morning inside this mysterious world.","The cool breeze drifted through the forest as birds chirped peacefully around the wooden house.","In the small training yard before the house, Noah stood opposite Akari.","She had already changed into a simpler blue kimono that allowed easier movement, while Noah held an steel sword in his right hand.","Akari folded her arms. \"Today, we’ll begin your weapon training.\"","Noah nodded attentively.","\"What weapon do you wish to specialize in?\"","\"Hmm...\" He thought for a moment. \"I’m comfortable with most weapons at a basic level. My best are swords and spears.\"","\"Then we’ll use the sword.\"","Akari raised her own blade from her storage ring.","It was a beautiful katana with a deep sapphire-blue sheath and a silver blade that gleamed beneath the morning light.","\"I’m strongest with the sword.\"","She rested its tip against the ground.","\"And remember this. The essence of all bladed weapons is fundamentally the same. If someone truly masters the sword, adapting to a spear, lance, rapier, dagger, or even an axe becomes much easier.\"","Noah raised an eyebrow.","\"Really?\"","She nodded.","\"They differ in reach, weight, and application. But balance, timing, distance, and technique...remain universal.\"","\"I understand.\"","Akari looked directly into his eyes.","\"Good. Then we’ll begin with the fundamentals.\"","She calmly raised one finger.","\"One thousand thrusts.\"","Another finger.","\"One thousand blocks.\"","A third.","\"One thousand parries.\"","Finally...","\"One thousand swings.\"","Noah stared blankly.","\"...What?\"","Akari maintained the same calm expression.","\"You heard me. Four thousand repetitions.\"","Noah almost dropped his sword.","\"That’s way too many!\"","Akari narrowed her eyes.","\"...Complaining already?\"","\"...\"","\"...No. But I am good at basics.\"","\"Yes. But it’s always best to be perfect in basics. If you are good then become better.\"","\"Okay.\" He accepted silently.","\"Then begin.\"","Noah let out a long sigh.","\"Yes, Master.\"","Swish!","Swish!","Swish!","Noah repeatedly thrust his sword forward. His movements were steady. Every thrust stopped at exactly the same position before smoothly returning.","’Damn! To think I needed to do same thing again. Life is so unfair!!’","Akari quietly watched from the side. For nearly an hour she said nothing. Just as Noah thought he was doing well.","\"No.\"","His shoulders instantly slumped.","\"...Already?\"","Akari walked toward him.","\"Your sword point trembles just before every thrust.\"","She gently adjusted his grip.","\"Relax your shoulders. You aren’t trying to stab through a mountain. The sword should move because your body guides it. Not because you’re forcing it.\"","She stepped back. \"Again.\"","\"Yes.\" he said and started to do it.","Swish!","Swish!","Swish!","This time Noah focused less on power. His thrusts immediately became smoother. Several hundred repetitions later. His breathing had become much more stable.","Sweat soaked his clothes. His arms burned. Yet he continued.","Akari finally gave a small nod.","\"Good. You’re improving.\"","A smile appeared on Noah’s face. Only for her next words to destroy it.","\"But your footing is still terrible.\"","\"...\"","After finishing the thousand thrusts. The blocking exercises began.","Tak!","Tak!","Tak!","Akari attacked with slow, controlled strikes.","Noah intercepted each one.","Clang!","Clang!","Clang!","His sword met hers repeatedly. But his body was aching from thousand thrusts.","’I can’t stop. I cannot look bad in her eyes. I need to be good. And amazing!!’","\"No.\"","She immediately stopped him again.","\"When you block... Don’t simply stop my sword. Control it.\"","She pushed lightly against his blade.","\"The moment our weapons touch... You should already be guiding mine away. Not meeting strength with strength.\"","She demonstrated. Their blades met. With one smooth circular motion, Akari redirected Noah’s sword completely off line.","Her own blade stopped at his throat.","\"So this...is a proper block.\"","Noah blinked. \"...That looked effortless.\"","He was amaze by her skills. She was just teaching him normal things. But now he wonder how strong was she while fighting with katana, using her whole powers. While he thought that, she spoke.","\"It should. The simpler the movement...The more refined the technique.\"","For the next several hundred repetitions. She corrected every tiny mistake.","His stance. His elbows. His wrists. Even his breathing. By the time the thousandth block ended.","Noah’s arms felt as though they no longer belonged to him. he took a small rest. Then afternoon was devoted to parrying.","Clang!","Clang!","Clang!","Unlike blocking parrying required far more precision. Rather than stopping the attack. He had to redirect it completely.","Again.","Again.","Again.","Every failed parry made Akari lightly tap him with the flat of her blade.","\"No.\"","\"You did it too early.\"","Again.","\"No. It was too late.\"","Again.","\"No. You are using too much force Noah.\"","He nodded and did it again, \"Is this enough?\"","\"Better.\" She said.","Hours passed. His wrists gradually began to ache. Every clash sent vibrations shooting up both arms.","Eventually Noah grimaced.","\"My wrists...\"","Akari looked at him briefly. Without saying a word, she tossed him a fruit.","He caught it.","\"...Thanks.\"","\"Eat it. That fruit will give you enough energy to continue further. We continue immediately afterward.\"","\"You’re terrifying.\" Noah said with tired voice. ’Damn, she can be scary..’","\"I’ve been told that before. But believe in me you will be lot stronger by doing this.\"","As evening approached. Only the swings remained. Compared to the previous exercises... This felt much more natural. He raised his sword.","Swish!","Again.","Swish!","Again.","Swish!","The movements flowed one after another.","Akari silently observed.","\"No.\"","Noah froze. \"...Seriously?\"","She walked toward him. \"You’re making the same mistake over and over.\"","He frowned. \"What mistake?\"","\"You’re obsessed with power.\" She stood before him. \"Every swing carries enough force to split a boulder. But afterwards...\"","She lightly poked his chest.","\"...you’re completely open.\"","’Father did said something similar.’","She slowly demonstrated. Her sword rose. Then descended. The movement was simple. It was elegant and effortless.","Noah tried his best not to look at her chest. He was good student. Not a pervert.","As he watch her he could tell there wasn’t an ounce of wasted strength. Yet the moment her swing ended. Her blade was already prepared for the next attack.","There was no pauses. There was no hesitation. No unnecessary movement.","\"This is what you should pursue.\"","She looked into Noah’s eyes.","\"A sword isn’t about swinging as hard as possible. It’s about never losing control. The technique should guide the power. Not the other way around. You are all tired now so don’t use too much power in swings.\"","Noah quietly stared at her demonstration.","For a long moment he said nothing. Then he slowly nodded.","\"...I understand.\"","A small smile appeared on Akari’s face.","\"Good. Then we’ll keep repeating these fundamentals.\"","\"Every day. Tomorrow we will only do one thousand thrusts. But afterwards i will teach you and fight with you all day to improve your thrust technique.\"","\"The day after that will be focus on blocks. then parries. And then swings. We will do that until I feel satisfied with your basics.\"","She sheathed her sword.","\"When those become second nature...We’ll begin teaching you real swordsmanship.\"","Noah looked at his trembling hands before letting out a helpless sigh.","\"...Why do all strong masters love making their disciples suffer?\"","Akari covered her mouth and laughed softly.","\"Hehe...Because the basics create the strongest warrior.\"","Noah looked at the sword in his hand. Then toward the smiling woman before him.","\"...Guess tomorrow’s going to hurt even more.\"","Akari’s smile widened.","\"It certainly will. Now it’s time to meditate and absorb mana. I have some mana cores of monsters. Very useful to you.\""]},{"number":263,"title":"Chapter 263: Daily Life With Akari [5]","paragraphs":["The next day.","Swish!","Swish!","Swish!","Noah’s sword thrust forward repeatedly.","This time, Akari allowed him to perform only one thousand thrusts. However that wasn’t the end of his training. After every hundred thrusts, she would personally spar with him.","Each time she effortlessly deflected his sword before pointing her blade at his throat.","\"No. Your thrust is too predictable.\"","Again.","\"Your wrist moved.\"","Again.","\"You shifted your weight too early.\"","Again.","\"You focused on speed instead of precision.\"","Even after his thousand thrust were completed, she continued to spar with him. By sunset, Noah had exchanged thousands of thrusts with her. His entire right arm had gone numb.","Yet his thrusts had become noticeably straighter. They were more stable and more efficient.","---","The third day.","Clang!","Clang!","Clang!","The entire day revolved around blocking.","Akari attacked from every possible angle.","Sometimes fast. Sometimes slow. Sometimes with deceptive feints. At first, Noah simply stopped her blade.","Every single time. She corrected him.","\"Don’t fight against the attack. Guide it. Control it. Steal your opponent’s balance.\"","\"As you say master.\" Noah never complained to her. If it was some old man teaching him. Then he might have asked and question many things. Just because he felt irritated. But here he believed in his dragon.","Gradually his sword stopped meeting hers head-on.","Instead it began redirecting incoming strikes with increasingly smoother movements.","\"You are fast learner.\"","By evening, Akari finally gave a satisfied nod.","\"Much better. You learned too fast.\"","The fourth day..","Parrying. The exercise Noah hated the most. Unlike blocking everything depended on timing.","If too early, he missed completely. If too late the attack landed. For hours, Akari attacked without mercy.","Clang!","Clang!","Clang!","Noah’s wrists screamed in pain. Whenever they became too swollen to continue.","Akari would gave him some time to rest.","He would complain sometimes.","\"We will continue soon.\"","\"You’re too cruel, Master.\"","’Though I love to see her fighting with sword. The way she move is just to beautiful to watch. And those slight bounce of her breasts. Hehe!’ He thought with evil grin.","\"I prefer disciplined. And what are you thinking? I don’t like that look you are having on face.\"","\"It’s nothing master. Just thinking how strong I will be after few months training with you.\"","She narrowed her eyes suspiciously. She knew he thought something bad but she just couldn’t prove it.","So they started again.","By sunset his parries had finally begun flowing naturally. For the first time he could redirect an attack using surprisingly little strength. And it was amazing since Akari was moving much faster than him.","With each day training They were becoming more close to each other.","---","The fifth day.","Swings.Compared to everything else. This should have been the easiest. Or so Noah believed. He was wrong.","\"You are being wide. But better than before.\"","He did again.","\"use little less strength.\"","Again.","\"You exposed your side., but that swing was good. A person equal to your power had taken the damage.\" She instructed.","Again.","\"You lost your balance.\"","Every swing was dissected. Every mistake corrected. Akari demonstrated each movement with astonishing elegance.","Her sword seemed to glide through the air effortlessly. No wasted motion. No unnecessary force. Watching her was almost like watching flowing water.","Noah tried to imitate her countless times.","By sunset his sword no longer whistled wildly through the air. Its path had become clean. Days slowly turned into weeks. Morning after morning. The peaceful forest echoed with the sound of steel.","Swish!","Clang!","Tak!","Akari remained as strict as ever.","She never praised Noah lightly. But every few days. She would quietly smile and say, \"Better.\"","That single word motivated Noah more than he expected. Whenever he made progress. She immediately increased the difficulty.","Even Akari was enjoying training Noah a lot. She never thought having disciple was so much amazing. And to her delight Noah was too much of fast learner.","Whenever he relaxed. She exposed another flaw. There was never an easy day. Yet Noah never complained again. He had already realized something.","Every correction she gave. Every seemingly endless repetition. Was steadily transforming his swordsmanship into something far more refined than brute strength alone. The foundation of a true swordsman was finally beginning to take shape.","After the doing training for whole day she would help him in mana control or provide him mana cores that she had collected over the months.","---","After two weeks of training under Akari.","Noah was finally on the verge of a breakthrough. He sat cross-legged in the yard beneath the quiet night sky.","A gentle blue aura enveloped his body as mana continuously flowed into his core. The mana core of a monster rested in his lap, its energy being steadily absorbed.","Inside his body, his core compressed further and further, forming an even denser layer of mana over it.","It had reached its limit. Sweat soaked his clothes as he gritted his teeth, enduring the pressure while forcing the breakthrough.","Crack.","Crack.","A faint cracking sound echoed from within his body.","Akari watched him silently from the porch of the house, a small smile resting on her lips.","BOOM!!","A gentle wave of mana burst outward from Noah, sweeping across the yard. He let out a long sigh of relief before slowly opening his eyes.","Akari walked over and stopped in front of him.","\"Congratulations on breaking through to the Condensed Core, Low stage.\"","Noah immediately stood up.","\"Yes!! I did it!\"","Unable to contain his excitement, he lunged forward and wrapped his arms around Akari in a tight embrace.","She was caught by surprise for a brief moment, but she didn’t push him away. Instead, she slowly wrapped her arms around him in return, feeling the warmth of another person’s embrace after so many years.","She gently rested her cheek against his shoulder while Noah buried his face in the crook of her neck.","He could feel her soft mounds pressed against his chest. But he was double happy. She allowed him to hug her.","’This is best breakthrough of my life!! I will get more close to her.’"]},{"number":264,"title":"Chapter 264: Third Petal","paragraphs":["Another day arrived.","Now that Noah had broken through to the Condensed Core (Low) stage, he was finally capable of learning the next form of his Weapon Art.","After informing Akari about it, she agreed to let him train by himself first.","Currently Noah stood alone in the open yard, his sword resting quietly in his right hand.","A gentle breeze drifted across the clearing, causing the surrounding leaves to rustle softly.","He slowly closed his eyes. The inheritance engraved within his mind began surfacing once again.","Frozen Lotus Blade Art.","Until now, he had mastered only two forms.","First Petal — Dewdrop Stance.","A stance that gathered every ounce of strength into a single perfectly balanced strike.","Second Petal — Still Surface Cut.","A nearly invisible slash of condensed frost capable of slicing through enemies before they even realized they had been attacked.","Now the third form appeared within his mind.","---","Third Petal — Petal Scatter (The Bloom Begins).","\"When the lotus sheds its first petals... the water remembers.\"","A stream of knowledge poured directly into Noah’s consciousness.","It wasn’t merely a description. There were sketches in his mind how to perfome this.","It was in detailed that he felt as if he was watching some swordsman perform it.","He focus on every movement. Every shift of the feet. Every rotation of the wrist.","Every flow of mana. Everything was engraved before his eyes. Slowly he opened his eyes. A sharp blue light flashed within them.","\"So this is how it’s done...\"","He took a deep breath. His feet shifted naturally into position. His left foot moved half a step forward.","His knees bent slightly. His shoulders relaxed. Mana quietly flowed from his core into his sword. The blade gradually became wrapped in a pale blue glow.","The third Petal was based on second Petal. So it was not that hard.","Noah slowly raised it. Then he swung.","Swish!","A beautiful crescent of frost shot forward. However only one appeared.","The second and third never formed.","The frost crescent flew a few meters before shattering into countless ice particles.","\"...Failed.\"","Noah wasn’t discouraged.","Instead, he replayed the inherited memory inside his head.","\"The first strike isn’t supposed to stop...\"","He realized his mistake immediately. This technique wasn’t composed of three separate attacks.","It was one continuous movement. Like flower petals scattering naturally through the wind.","Everything had to flow together. He adjusted his footing once more. Mana circulated calmly through his meridians.","This time he moved without hesitation.","Swish!","The first slash swept outward. Before it had completely finished. His body rotated naturally.","Swish!","A second arc followed immediately behind the first.","Without stopping his sword completed another elegant rotation.","Swish!","The third strike flowed as smoothly as running water.","Three pale-blue crescents finally emerged.","They resembled translucent lotus petals drifting gracefully through the air.","They were beautiful. Yet carrying astonishing killing intent. The petals spiraled outward before flying across the yard.","Unfortunately only the first remained stable. The second dispersed halfway through its flight.","The third shattered almost immediately after leaving his blade.","Noah lowered his sword.","\"Closer.\"","From the side Akari quietly observed everything.","She didn’t interrupt him. She merely watched. She could clearly tell Noah wasn’t simply memorizing movements.","He was understanding them. Hours slowly passed.","Again.","Swish!","Again.","Swish! Swish! Swish!","Again.","Again.","Again.","The yard echoed endlessly with the sound of his sword cutting through the air.","Sweat gradually soaked his clothes. His breathing became heavier. The mana inside his core steadily decreased.","Yet Noah never stopped. Each failure revealed another flaw. Sometimes his timing was off. Sometimes the second strike carried too much strength.","Other times the mana between the three slashes wasn’t distributed evenly.","Every mistake forced him to refine the technique further.","As the afternoon sun slowly descended.","His body once again started to feel the pain and ache in muscles. Each moments felt like they were tearing his muscles. Even after weeks of training non stop. He wasn’t used to it. Rather if he felt no pain he would feel unsatisfied with his training.","Something finally changed.","Noah’s movements became noticeably smoother.","His body no longer paused between attacks. The three slashes flowed together like a single graceful dance.","Mana surged through his blade. His eyes narrowed.","\"This time...\" His breathing slightly heavy.","His foot stepped forward. His sword danced.","Swish!","Swish!","Swish!","Three glowing frost crescents burst forth simultaneously.","Unlike before they remained perfectly intact.","Semi-transparent. Pale blue. They spun through the air like lotus petals drifting away from a flower in full bloom.","They were elegant, beautiful, and deadly.","The three frost crescents spiraled outward like drifting lotus petals before suddenly changing direction.","Rather than flying aimlessly, they curved gracefully through the air and converged upon the exact spot Noah imagined his opponent had occupied only moments earlier.","The instant they struck.","BOOM!!","A deafening explosion of frost erupted across the training ground.","Crack! Crack! Crack!","The earth split apart as an overwhelming wave of freezing energy surged in every direction.","A thick sheet of ice spread rapidly over the ground, swallowing everything in its path before blooming outward in the shape of enormous lotus petals.","Jagged ice crystals burst from the frozen earth, while a cloud of glittering frost rose into the air.","The surrounding trees trembled violently from the impact, their leaves instantly coated in a thin layer of white frost.","A chilling wind swept through the yard as countless ice particles drifted downward like shimmering snow.","Noah stood silently, staring at the destruction before him.","A slow smile spread across his face.","\"It won’t take much longer before I truly master it.\"","Although he still lacked speed, power, and precision...","The Third Petal—Petal Scatter had finally begun to bloom.","---","Evening settled over the yard. The sky glowed soft orange, though the sun itself was not present in sky.","After all day hard training, Noah was finally resting in what he believed to be the most peaceful place in the world.","Noah lay on the wooden veranda after a long day of training his third form. His head rested on the soft lap of his master, Akari.","She sat in seiza, knees folded neatly beneath her, wearing a dark violet kimono that looked almost black in the fading light.","Her black hair was tied up in a neat bun, a few loose strands brushing against the fair skin of her neck and scales.","Those calm blue eyes looked down at him with quiet fondness. Her fingers moved slowly through his snow-white hair, gentle and steady.","\"You’re getting bolder every day,\" she said, a soft smile touching her lips. \"Asking for a lap pillow out of nowhere...\""]},{"number":265,"title":"Chapter 265: She’s... Taking My Side","paragraphs":["The kimono sat a little loose around her shoulders. From where Noah rested, the soft, huge curve of her breasts made it hard to see her face clearly. He didn’t mind. Not at all.","He turned his head slightly and rubbed his cheek against her thigh. The firm warmth of her legs felt grounding and comforting at the same time.","\"I wanted this for a while,\" he admitted quietly. \"I just never had the courage. But we’ve grown closer... so I thought, why not?\"","Akari gave a small, amused breath. \"You’re acting like a kid. Does something so simple from an old woman like me really make you that happy?\"","Noah immediately opened one eye and looked up at her.","\"What are you talking about? Being treated this kindly by someone as breathtakingly beautiful as you is something most men could only dream about.\"","She chuckled under her breath, the sound low and warm. \"There you go again with the compliments. Always trying to flatter me.\"","\"I’m only saying what’s true.\"","Her hand continued its slow path through his hair. \"In that case... you can ask me for this anytime after training.\"","Noah’s chest tightened with quiet joy.","He couldn’t help thinking how strange fate truly was. When he had first arrived in this mysterious world, he believed he had been trapped in the worst possible situation.","Now each passing day made him wonder if it had been a blessing in disguise. He slowly closed his eyes again.","’She’s unbelievably kind. I really like her and being around her. If this continues... A few more months together. I might genuinely fall for her.’","Noah’s brain had already begun to imagine a future in which they both remained here for years.","They would slowly fall for each other. Then one day, in the heat of the moment, they would cross the line.","They wouldn’t stop there, they would keep going. And the result of their actions would be born into this world.","Someone who would call him Dad and her Mom.","A soft, almost silly laugh slipped out of him. \"Hehe~\"","Akari tilted her head, curious. She leaned forward a little. The softness of her breasts pressed fully against his cheek and the side of his face. The sensation he felt was warm and soft.","The thin kimono did little to hide the heat of her skin or the gentle give of her flesh. The light scent of her body wrapped around him was sweet.","\"What is it?\" she asked, voice soft near his ear. \"Why are you laughing like that?\"","Noah’s cheeks felt warm. \"I just... feel like the luckiest man alive right now.\"","He forced himself to stay still. He controled himself from thinking by his lower body.","Akari’s gentle giggle made her chest shift lightly against him. \"You’re strange, Noah.\"","He drew in a slow breath, trying to steady the flutter in his chest. He didn’t want to seem childish. Not when something more serious waited on his tongue.","\"Akari...\" His voice dropped, it was more careful. \"There’s something I’ve been keeping from you. Something important.\"","She sensed the change in him at once. Her hand stilled in his hair for a moment, then resumed its soft strokes.","\"What is it, Noah?\"","He looked up at her, heart steadying, ready at last to speak the truth about Ophelia... and about himself.","\"Actually... it’s about Ophelia.\" Noah’s voice grew quieter. \"I didn’t tell you everything about her. I hid a few things.\"","The gentle atmosphere between them vanished. Akari’s expression slowly turned serious.","\"What is it, Noah?\"","Even her voice had become calm and solemn.","Noah took a deep breath before gathering his courage.","\"Actually...Ophelia and I were engaged.She was my fiancée.\"","The moment those words left his mouth, Akari’s eyes widened. She remained silent for several moments before finally speaking.","\"Noah...I would have been happy to hear that.\"","She looked down at him. \"A man like you becoming my daughter’s fiancé... I would have gladly accepted it.\"","Her brows slowly knitted together.","\"But...what do you mean by were? Are you saying the engagement no longer exists?\"","Noah slowly nodded.","\"Yes. It was broken.\" He lowered his gaze. \"She... never loved me.\"","\"I loved her...\" He felt bitterness in his mouth while saying that. Not because of sad memories, but saying he loved her was really repulsive to him since he really dislike her.","’Though it was not me but past Noah who loved her.’","\"but she never felt the same. And then...\"","After taking another deep breath...","Noah began telling her everything.The ridicule he endured afterward.","He hid nothing this time.He spoke honestly from beginning to end.","When he finally finished. Silence filled the veranda. Only the gentle evening breeze could be heard.","His head still rested on Akari’s lap.","\"...Akari?\"","He called her softly.","She didn’t answer immediately. Several long moments passed. Finally. \"Noah...\"","Her voice was frighteningly calm. A chill ran down Noah’s spine.","\"W-What is it?\"","Akari’s hands slowly clenched the fabric of her kimono.","\"Did my daughter...truly do all of that?\"","Her voice carried a restrained anger Noah had never heard before.","He nodded slowly.","\"Yes...I know I wasn’t completely innocent either. I was drunk... But I never intended to hurt her. I never wanted anything like that to happen.\"","\"Enough.\"","Akari interrupted him.","\"I’ve spent these past few weeks with you. I know the kind of person you are.\"","Her usually gentle eyes were now filled with unmistakable anger.","\"I cannot believe that my own daughter falsely accused you of assault just because she didn’t like you.\"","She closed her eyes briefly, taking a slow breath to calm herself.","When she opened them again the anger remained. Only now it was hidden beneath perfect composure.","Slowly she lowered her hand and gently cupped Noah’s cheek.","Her fingers softly stroked his face.","\"Oh, Noah...\"","Her voice had become incredibly gentle.","\"It must have been so painful. To be accused by by the person you loved...To lose your engagement...to be exiled from your own family...And to endure everyone’s scorn because of a lie.\"","Her thumb lightly brushed across his cheek.","\"I can only imagine how lonely you must have felt.\"","Noah stared at her in complete disbelief.","’She’s... taking my side?Wait... really?Damn! It was not me... though now I have all memories of Noah. I do feel like that everything happened to me.’","He had expected anger. He had expected her to defend her daughter.","Instead the first thing she worried about was him.","---","[A/N:Don’t worry guys I won’t drag it. Soon I will make sure to end this small arc!!]"]},{"number":266,"title":"Chapter 266: Unexpected Actions","paragraphs":["’This woman... she’s the best.’","Noah couldn’t help smiling.","Unable to contain the warmth swelling inside his chest, he turned slightly and buried his face against the side of her waist where the wide obi was wrapped around her kimono.","One arm slipped gently around her waist as he rubbed his cheek against the soft fabric.","\"Akari... you’re the best. Thank you. I honestly thought you’d be angry with me.\"","\"Ahn? N-Noah... what are you doing?\"","Akari’s composed expression instantly crumbled.","Her sapphire-blue eyes widened in surprise as she looked down at the young man clinging to her like a spoiled child.","\"Hehe... Just... let me stay like this for a little longer.\"","He rested his face against her obi, enjoying the comforting warmth that surrounded her.","Akari let out a helpless sigh.","\"You really are acting like a child today. Maybe I am... But I can’t help it. Besides...\"","He smiled against her waist.","\"You don’t seem to hate it.\"","She blinked. After a brief hesitation, her hand slowly came to rest atop his head Her fingers gently combed through his snow-white hair.","A faint smile appeared on her lips.","\"No. I suppose I don’t.\"","For some reason...","Watching Noah behave so openly around her filled her heart with an indescribable warmth.","It wasn’t bothersome. If anything she found it strangely comforting. After another quiet moment, Noah finally released her and sat upright.","Now they were facing each other. Separated by only a short distance.","Noah quietly looked into her eyes. Those clear sapphire-blue eyes shimmered like a tranquil ocean beneath the evening sky.","Long eyelashes framed them beautifully.","The orange glow of the setting evening bathed her porcelain skin in a warm light, making her already graceful features appear even softer.","A few loose strands of raven-black hair swayed gently across her cheeks.","The dark sapphire scales along both sides of her neck and across her right cheek reflected the fading sunlight like polished gemstones. The natural pink of her lips, soft as rose petals with no need for color.","He was mesmerized by her.","Noah found himself unable to look away. He had noticed it during the past few weeks.","The longer he stayed beside her. The more beautiful she seemed to become. Was she truly becoming more beautiful. Or was it simply because of the feelings quietly growing within his heart?","Ba-dump.","Ba-dump.","Ba-dump.","His heartbeat echoed loudly inside his chest.","\"Noah?\"","Akari tilted her head slightly. Her soft palm gently touched his cheek.","\"What are you thinking? You’ve been staring at me for quite a while.\"","Noah smiled. Slowly he raised his own hand. His fingers lightly rested against her cheek.","His thumb gently traced the smooth sapphire scales beneath her eye.","The scales were cool to the touch. Firm yet strangely beautiful. A faint blush slowly spread across Akari’s cheeks.","\"W-What are you doing all of a sudden?\"","She looked away for a moment before meeting his gaze again.","\"It’s... embarrassing.\"","Being gently caressed by her own disciple. It was a feeling she had never imagined experiencing.","\"Noah...\"","He softly called her name.","\"Akari.\"","\"Yes?\"","She looked directly into his eyes. The way he was looking at her was something she was getting first time from him.","Never before had someone looked at her with such warmth and such tenderness. Perhaps her parents once had. But Noah’s gaze was different. It carried something she couldn’t quite understand.","\"You know...\"","He smiled gently.","\"I’ve been wanting to give you something. For always being so kind to me. For taking care of me...And for believing me.\"","Akari tilted her head again, unconsciously pressing her cheek a little further into his palm.","The gesture made her appear unexpectedly adorable.","\"What could you possibly give me?\"","She smiled softly.","\"I don’t need anything, Noah. Honestly...Having you beside me after all these years...is already more than enough. It makes me so much happy.\"","Her eyes shimmered gently as she spoke.","Then without realizing it. She closed her eyes and leaned ever so slightly into his touch.","Noah felt his heart skip a beat. He swallowed nervously.","This was too much for him. How could he handle this. At this time he really wanted to keep this woman only for himself.","\"Akari...\"","\"Hm?\"","She slowly opened her eyes again.","\"What is—\"","Noah smiled apologetically.","\"...I’m sorry.\"","Before she could ask what he meant. He gently cupped the side of her face.","Then leaned forward.","Chuu~","His lips softly brushed against her left cheek. It lasted only a brief moment.","It was gentle and light. Filled only with gratitude and affection.","The evening breeze swept across the yard. Flower petals drifted quietly between them.","Akari’s eyes widened completely. She remained frozen. Her mind blank.","By the time she finally reacted. Noah had already leaped to his feet.","\"Hehe! S-Sorry!\"","He scratched the back of his head awkwardly before hurriedly running toward the other side of the house.","Leaving her sitting there alone.","Akari silently watched him disappear around the corner. Her fingers slowly rose to touch the place where his lips had rested.","She stared into space. Unable to process what had just happened.","\"W... What...?\"","Color rapidly flooded her cheeks.","In only a few seconds. Her entire face had turned crimson like some tomato.","The usual cold and strict Akari was feeling embarrassed? Someone who had lived alone for so many years, she was actually feeling flustered.","\"H-He...He kissed me...\"","Who kissed her last time? It was her daughter Ophelia. And now it was a young man who was similar to Ophelia’s age.","Her voice came out as little more than a whisper. She covered both burning cheeks with her hands.","\"W-What in the world was that...? T-That’s completely improper...How could he suddenly kiss me...? And why am I acting like this?\"","Her thoughts became a complete mess.","She was a Sovereign-ranked warrior. Someone capable of reacting to lightning-fast attacks.","Yet she hadn’t stopped him. Not because she couldn’t. But because for that brief moment.","She simply hadn’t wanted to move. Wondering what he wanted to do. Realizing that only made her face grow even redder.","\"N-No... Damn! I am such idiot.\"","She shook her head repeatedly.","\"I shouldn’t be thinking like this. This is... this is far too dangerous.\"","Yet despite all the embarrassment overwhelming her. Her fingertips never left the place where Noah had kissed her.","As if she wished to preserve that tiny warmth for just a little while longer.","---","The next few hours were rather awkward for both of them.","Neither Noah nor Akari brought up what had happened. Not even during dinner.","The meal was unusually quiet.","The only sounds were the gentle clinking of their wooden bowls and the soft evening breeze drifting through the open doorway.","After dinner, Noah stepped outside to meditate.","He sat beneath a tree, quietly absorbing the abundant mana flowing through the surrounding nature.","Meanwhile Akari silently returned to her room.","In one corner lay the simple bed she had made— a thick layer of dried grass and leaves, covered with a large fresh leaf that served as bedding.","She lay down upon it and slowly closed her eyes.","Yet the gentle kiss Noah had placed upon her cheek refused to leave her thoughts.","Every time she tried to clear her mind. She could almost feel that fleeting warmth against her skin again.","She slowly turned onto her side.","’...How am I supposed to react? Should I have said something during dinner? But... what could I have possibly said? It was improper... It was wrong...Yet...","She sighed quietly. ’I’m not angry with him... Why?’","Her thoughts only became more tangled. Was it because she had lived alone for sixty years? Had loneliness changed her so much that she no longer understood how she was supposed to react?","The questions continued to circle inside her mind. While Akari struggled with her thoughts.","The wooden door quietly slid open.","Creak","Noah stepped inside as quietly as possible. The room was illuminated by the pale silver light filtering through the open window.","A gentle breeze drifted inside, causing the loose strands of Akari’s black hair to sway softly.","Noah glanced toward her.","’She appeared to be asleep.’ He thought.","Her breathing was slow and even. Carefully, trying not to wake her, he walked over to the bed. Then he quietly lay down beside her. Both of them were sleeping on their sides.","Facing each other. He slowly inched a little closer. Close enough to admire her peaceful sleeping face.","\"She’s asleep.\"","A small smile appeared on his lips. He remained silent for a while before letting out a quiet sigh.","\"I’m sorry, Akari. I should apologize properly tomorrow. I wanted to during dinner...but I got nervous.And honestly...\"","He laughed awkwardly to himself. \"I thought you’d scold me. Maybe even hit me. But... you didn’t.\"","He looked at her sleeping face for another moment.","Unable to resist he slowly raised one finger. His fingertip gently touched the tip of her nose before lightly rubbing it.","\"Hehe... You really do look adorable when you’re asleep.\""]},{"number":267,"title":"Chapter 267: Can I Get a Reward?","paragraphs":["\"Hehe... You really do look adorable when you’re asleep.\"","His gaze softened. \"I kind of want to kiss you again.\"","He quickly shook his head. \"No. What is this? Some strange chemical reaction inside the human body? People feel attracted to someone and then call it a crush... or love?\"","He frowned thoughtfully.","\"I’m definitely attracted to her. But don’t misunderstand that as love, Noah. Maybe not yet.\"","He fell silent. After another long moment, he smiled faintly. \"Still. I really care about her. I hope one day... I’ll be able to fall asleep while hugging her. And cuddling with her.\"","A lazy yawn escaped him. His eyelids slowly grew heavier. Within minutes he quietly drifted off to sleep.","Silence returned to the room.","Akari slowly opened her eyes. Her blue gaze immediately landed on Noah’s sleeping face. He was much closer than before.","\"This man...\"","Her cheeks instantly turned bright red. She hadn’t been asleep at all. She had merely kept her eyes closed. And this shameless young man had spent the entire time saying such embarrassing things right beside her.","\"This man...\"","She clenched her fists beneath the blanket. \"Tomorrow. I’m going to train him much harder. Hmph!\"","She firmly closed her eyes again. Yet one sentence stubbornly echoed inside her mind.","\"I hope one day... I’ll be able to fall asleep while hugging her. And cuddling with her.\"","\"Argh...\"","She buried her burning face on her both palm. Rolling from one side to the other several times.","\"How am I supposed to sleep after hearing something like that...?\"","For the first time in many years. Akari found herself completely unable to fall asleep.","---","The next morning, Akari woke up early.","After freshening up, she quietly sat in the living room, enjoying the peaceful silence of the morning.","Not long afterward Noah came to room.","\"Akari!!\"","His cheerful voice came from behind. He walked over and sat down directly in front of her, making her flinch slightly.","\"Y-Yes?What is it?\" She tried her best to maintain her usual composed expression.","Without saying another word, Noah lowered his head deeply.","\"I’m really sorry for kissing you.\"","Akari’s eyelids twitched.","’Why would he say it so openly...? He could have simply apologized, and I would have understood... Now he had bluntly spoken the entire incident aloud.’","Seeing the guilt and nervousness written across his face, she let out a helpless sigh. She had never truly been angry with him.","\"It’s alright. I’m not angry. So you don’t have to keep apologizing.\"","A small smile appeared on her lips. \"I’m just glad you understand that it wasn’t appropriate.\"","Noah slowly looked up. Relief filled his blue eyes.","\"Akari...Thank you. You’re far too kind to me.\"","She smiled gently.","\"Come now. Don’t keep feeling guilty over it.\"","Noah nodded repeatedly.","\"Thank you again.\"","A grin suddenly appeared on his face.","\"So... does that mean I can kiss you again sometime in the future? Since you didn’t seem to hate it.\"","Silence.","A vein visibly throbbed on Akari’s forehead. Yet she somehow maintained her smile.","\"...Noah.\"","He looked at her expectantly.","\"Yes?\"","She slowly stood up. \"Let’s begin today’s training. I’ve prepared something new for you. A new training?\"","Noah immediately stood as well. Before he could ask anything else.","Akari walked over, grabbed him effortlessly, and hoisted him over her right shoulder like a sack of rice.","\"W-Wait! Master!What are you doing?!\"","Whenever training was involved, Noah naturally addressed her as \"Master.\"","Now he hung upside down over her shoulder, completely helpless.","She raised her left hand and slap on his ass sharply.","Smack!","\"Ahh! Master! That hurt!\"","His face instantly turned bright red from embarrassment.","’Dammit! I was just joking,how can she just spank me for it.’ He thought shamefully.","Akari gave him another firm smack.","\"Don’t talk. I forgave you. And yet you still had the nerve to ask if you could kiss me again. How shameless can you possibly be?\"","\"W-Wait, Master! I was only joking to lighten the mood!\"","He tried to give her reason for it.","\"Hmph.\" But she was not in mood to listen. Blue lightning crackled around her body. The next instant.","Crack!","She vanished.","No she was simply moving so fast that Noah couldn’t perceive her. She shot through the forest like a streak of blue lightning.","Meanwhile Noah’s world spun violently.","\"I... think...I’m going to throw up...\"","---","Several minutes later.","\"Cough!\"","\"Cough!\"","Noah leaned against a nearby tree for support.","His face had gone pale. The entire world continued spinning around him.","He shook his head repeatedly, trying to regain his senses.","Only after several moments did the dizziness finally lessen.","He slowly turned toward Akari. She stood nearby with her usual calm expression.","As though carrying someone at terrifying speed had been completely normal.","Noah swallowed nervously.","\"So... Master... What’s this new training?\"","Akari raised one eyebrow before smiling faintly.","\"This place is far away from our house.\"","Noah blinked.","’Our house?’","For some reason hearing those words made him smile inwardly.","She continued. \"This forest contains numerous monsters. Most of them are around D+ Rank.\"","Noah nodded.","\"Alright. So what do you want me to do? You’ll remain inside this forest for the next week.\"","His eyes widened.","\"...What?\"","\"You heard me correctly. You’ll survive here for seven days. Fight monsters. Run if necessary. Find food. Build shelter. Do whatever it take to survive.\"","She looked directly into his eyes.","\"And this time... I won’t help you. Even if your life is in danger.\"","Her voice remained calm. But Noah could clearly hear the lingering annoyance from this morning. She was telling those last words in annoyance.","\"Now go.\"","Noah silently looked toward the dense forest.","Then back at her.","\"Alright. I’ll do it.\"","He paused for a moment before smiling.","\"But... Can I get a reward after I finish? It would be much more motivating.\"","Akari folded her arms.","\"A reward? Hmm... I suppose that’s reasonable. I’ll think of something.\"","Noah immediately shook his head.","\"How about this? You simply grant me one wish.\"","Akari frowned.","\"...One wish? What exactly do you want?\"","Her eyes narrowed suspiciously.","\"And for heaven’s sake...don’t even think about asking to give a kiss to me again.\"","Her cheeks flushed ever so slightly.","Noah couldn’t help laughing.","\"Relax, Master. I won’t ask for something like that. It’s nothing outrageous. I promise.\"","She continued staring at him for several seconds.","Finally she sighed.","\"Fine. As long as it isn’t something I dislike...I’ll grant it.\"","Noah’s smile widened.","\"Thank you, Master. Then I’ll be going.\"","Akari gave a small nod.","\"Good. Also even if you are trying to survive. Don’t forget to train. Especially Aura. That’s I have been teaching you. Of course it’s something that might take you a years to learn. But still keep practicing.\"","\"Yes Master! I won’t neglect my training.\"","With last nod a blue lightning danced around her body once more.","Crack!","She disappeared into the distance. Leaving Noah alone before the vast forest.","He looked toward the endless trees ahead. A confident smirk slowly spread across his face.","\"One week...Let’s survive.\"","With that, he tightened his grip on his sword and walked into the forest.","---","The dense forest welcomed Noah with complete silence.","The air was damp.","Noah moved cautiously through the undergrowth.","Unlike before, he wasn’t in a hurry. This week wasn’t about reaching a destination.","It was about surviving.","His blue eyes carefully scanned his surroundings while mana quietly circulated through his body.","Only ten minutes had passed.","Rustle...","Rustle...","A strange sound echoed from a bush several meters ahead.","Noah immediately stopped.","His right hand moved to the hilt of his sword. The forest became silent once again.","Hissssss—!!","A massive serpent burst out from the bushes.","It was over eight meters long.","Its body was covered in dark green scales patterned with black stripes that blended perfectly with the surrounding vegetation.","Its golden slit pupils locked onto Noah.","Two long venomous fangs protruded from its mouth as its forked tongue flickered repeatedly through the air.","The monster slowly raised the front half of its body.","It towered nearly three meters above the ground.","It looked around D- Rank monster.","The snake hissed once more before shooting toward Noah with astonishing speed.","Noah remained calm.","A smile appeared on his face. \"Let’s see how much I’ve improved.\"","Mana surged through his core. His left hand stretched toward the incoming serpent.","Crack!","Crack!","Massive pillars of ice erupted from the ground around the serpent.","Before it could react, thick frozen bars rapidly connected together.","A giant cage of crystal-clear ice had formed around the monster. The serpent slammed against the frozen prison.","BOOM!","The entire cage trembled violently. Cracks spread across a few sections.","But it remained intact. The monster hissed furiously, repeatedly smashing its massive body against the walls. It’s body caught tightly with coldness. Some ice started spread over it’s scales.","Noah didn’t give it another chance. Mana flowed into his sword. A layer of frost coated the blade until it glowed with a pale blue light.","He stepped forward. His figure disappeared in a blur.","Swish!","One clean slash. The sword flashed past the serpent’s neck.","Slice!","The enormous head slowly separated from its body.","Dark blood sprayed across the frozen cage.","The severed head struck the ground with a heavy thud while the remaining body violently convulsed before collapsing.","Silence returned to the forest.","---","While Noah began his seven-day survival training, Akari remained far from his position.","She sat alone in a quiet clearing, surrounded by silence.","Her eyes were gently closed as the sapphire scales adorning her neck and cheek quivered ever so slightly, trembling as if responding to an unseen force flowing through her body.","A few moments later, she slowly opened her eyes.","A faint, genuine smile graced her lips.","\"I’m close... once again I am so close to fully awakening and comtrolling my bloodline.\"","She lowered her gaze to her trembling hand before softly clenching it into a fist.","\"Just a few more months... and I’ll be able to control it completely without losing myself to madness like before.\""]},{"number":268,"title":"Chapter 268: Survival Training","paragraphs":["\"What the hell is this?\"","Noah stood at the edge of an entirely different section of the forest, staring ahead with a mixture of confusion and fascination.","He had finally passed through the seemingly endless woodland of towering trees, only to find himself standing before something even stranger.","A forest of mushrooms. And not ordinary mushrooms.","They were enormous.","Some stood three or four meters tall, while others towered high enough to rival small trees. Their thick beige stalks rose from the damp earth, supporting broad umbrella-shaped caps covered in irregular white patterns.","Noah slowly stepped between them, looking around in amazement.","\"Now this really looks like some fairy-tale forest.\"","The deeper he walked, the stranger the scenery became.","Huge mushrooms surrounded him from every direction, their overlapping caps blocking much of the sunlight and casting pale shadows across the ground.","\"Damn... There was some cartoon movie with tiny blue creatures that used mushrooms as houses, wasn’t there?\"","Noah muttered thoughtfully, remembering something from his childhood. Those memories didn’t belong to Noah Eldritch. They belonged to his previous life on Earth.","Back when his greatest concerns had been school, games, movies, and deciding what he wanted to watch after getting home.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","Shake...","Noah abruptly stopped.","\"...Hm?\"","His smile disappeared. He slowly turned his head toward the right. One particular mushroom stood several meters away.","Noah narrowed his eyes. \"Was that my imagination...\"","He stared at it suspiciously.","\"...or did that mushroom just move?\"","Nothing happened. The giant mushroom remained completely still. Noah continued staring at it for several seconds.","Then he made the wisest decision he could think of. He turned around.","\"Fuck this. I’m not taking any chances.\"","And ran. The instant he started running—","SHAKE!","Every mushroom around him suddenly trembled.","Noah’s eyes widened.","\"Of course!\"","The enormous caps began violently shaking.","Puff! Puff! Puff!","Clouds of fine powder erupted from beneath them. White dust poured into the air from every direction, rapidly covering the entire path in a thick haze.","\"Shit!\"","Noah immediately raised his forearm, covering his nose and mouth as he sprinted forward. Unfortunately he was already too late. Some of the strange powder had entered his nose.","\"Cough! Cough!\"","Noah coughed violently. His throat burned. Then something even worse happened. It felt as though his blood had begun boiling inside his veins.","\"What the—?!\"","Then came the itching. Noah’s eyes nearly popped out of their sockets. It started around his neck. Then his arms. His chest. His back.","Within seconds, almost every part of his body felt as though thousands of tiny insects were crawling beneath his skin.","\"F-FUCK!!\"","The urge to scratch himself was unbearable. Noah clenched his teeth and forced himself to continue running.","Mana surged toward his legs.","Boom!","His speed increased sharply. At the same time, a thin layer of frost spread across the exposed portions of his skin.","The cold slightly numbed his nerves. But only slightly.","\"Who the hell designed these things?!\"","He continued sprinting through the mushroom forest. Behind him, more gigantic mushrooms began trembling.","Puff!","Another cloud of spores exploded into the air. The entire forest seemed to have awakened.","Noah lowered his head and ran faster.","He couldn’t keep his mouth covered anymore. He needed both arms for balance while sprinting through the uneven terrain.","Which meant, \"Cough! Cough! FUCK!\"","He inhaled even more spores. The itching intensified. His eyes watered. His skin became increasingly red beneath the thin layer of frost.","RUMBLE!","The ground beneath him suddenly trembled.","Noah’s expression changed.","\"Wait...\"","His right foot sank. Then his left.","Squelch!","Within seconds, both legs had sunk almost to his knees.","\"What?!\"","Noah looked down. The previously solid ground had transformed into thick, muddy sludge.","\"No fucking way!\"","A swamp. The mushrooms hadn’t merely released poisonous or irritating spores. They had somehow altered the ground beneath him as well. And he was sinking.","Noah immediately stretched out his hand.","CRACK!","Ice erupted beneath his submerged feet. Instead of trying to freeze the entire swamp, Noah concentrated his mana into a single structure. A thick pillar of ice formed beneath him.","It extended downward until it struck solid earth.","BOOM!","The pillar rapidly expanded upward.","Noah was launched out of the swamp.","\"Whoa—!\"","His body flew several meters through the air.","He twisted himself awkwardly before crashing onto solid ground.","Thud!","He rolled twice. Then immediately pushed himself back onto his feet.","He just run.","Mana flooded into his legs again. Noah shot forward. His breathing became ragged.","His skin burned. His entire body was screaming at him to stop and scratch himself.","\"Just a little farther...\"","Through watery eyes, he finally saw it. The end of this damned mushroom forest.","\"Just a little more!\"","Noah pushed himself harder.","PUFF!","Another enormous cloud of spores erupted.","\"NOPE!\"","He lunged forward with everything he had.","Thud!","Noah crossed the boundary and crashed into the ordinary forest beyond. He rolled across the grass several times before finally stopping.","For perhaps two seconds there was silence.","\"FUCK! FUCK! FUCK!!\"","Noah began furiously scratching his arms. His whole body. Anywhere his hands could reachThe itching was maddening.","\"ARGHH! WHY DOES IT ITCH SO MUCH?!\"","His nails dragged across his skin hard enough to leave red marks. Realizing he was going to tear his own skin apart if he continued, Noah forced himself to stop.","\"Cold... Cold!\"","Mana surged from his core. A thin layer of ice rapidly formed across his entire body. Coldness seeped into his skin. It helped but barely.","Noah collapsed onto his back. For the next ten minutes, he simply suffered.","Clenching his teeth and rolling his body around. Occasionally scratching himself before desperately forcing his hands away again.","The unbearable itching began to fade. Noah remained sprawled across the ground, staring blankly at the canopy above him.","\"Haah...\"","His chest rose and fell rapidly.","\"Haah... haah...\"","His clothes were dirty. His hair was a mess. His skin was covered in red scratch marks. There were even tears at the corners of his eyes.","But Noah had survived. More importantly he had preserved something precious.","Noah slowly raised one trembling fist toward the sky.","\"I...\"","His lips quivered.","\"...I fucking did it.\"","A tear rolled down his cheek.","\"I didn’t scratch my crotch...\"","For several seconds, Noah simply lay there in solemn silence, appreciating what might have been his greatest achievement since arriving in this world.","Then he covered his face with both hands.","\"Fuck...\"","He had been stabbed, burned, thrown through walls, and almost eaten alive.","Yet today Noah learned something important. There were forms of suffering that could rival pain itself.","And apparently unbearable itching was one of them."]},{"number":269,"title":"Chapter 269: New Clue?","paragraphs":["\"Fuck my luck.\"","His sword immediately appeared in his hand.","He lowered his body into a combat stance, gripping the hilt firmly as his eyes swept across the enemies ahead.","\"Well...\"","A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"It’s better than itching.\"","Nine enormous bears stood before him.","They resembled ordinary black bears at first glance, but each was nearly twice the size of a normal adult bear.","Their bodies were packed with thick muscles beneath coarse black fur, while enormous claws extended from their paws.","Drool dripped from their jaws. Eighteen crimson eyes remained locked onto Noah.","GRRROOOAAARRR!!","The largest bear suddenly roared. And that was all the others needed.","THUD! THUD! THUD!","Nine massive bodies charged simultaneously. The earth trembled beneath their weight.","Noah tightened his grip on his sword. Mana surged from his newly advanced Condensed Core.","A pale-blue aura enveloped his body, strengthening his muscles as additional mana flowed into his sword.","A thin line of frost formed along its edge. His left foot slid forward. His breathing steadied.","\"Come.\"","The first three bears were already closing in.","Noah moved..His sword swept through the air.","Three times rapidly.","Swish! Swish! Swish!","Frozen Lotus Blade Art.","[Third Petal — Petal Scatter]","Three semi-transparent crescents of compressed frost emerged from his blade.","They resembled enormous pale-blue lotus petals. For an instant, the three frost crescents scattered in different directions.","The bears continued charging. One attempted to move left. Another rushed straight ahead.","The third suddenly changed direction. Yet the frost petals didn’t follow them.","Instead they curved backward.","Their trajectories converged upon the positions the monsters had occupied only moments earlier.","And because several more bears were charging directly through those same positions.","The three petals struck.","BOOOOM!!","A violent explosion of frost shook the forest.","CRACK! CRACK! CRACK!","Ice spread explosively across the ground.","The earth cracked beneath the sudden drop in temperature as enormous crystalline formations erupted upward.","\"GRRRAAAHHH!!\"","Several bears roared in pain.","One frost crescent sliced deeply through a bear’s abdomen before detonating, instantly coating half its body in ice.","Another struck a second bear across the shoulder.","The third exploded between two charging monsters.","BOOM!!","Blood sprayed across the frozen earth.","One bear collapsed immediately.","Another stumbled several steps before falling, its hind legs trapped beneath thick layers of ice.","The third had its front leg nearly severed.","\"Only one dead?!\"","Noah’s expression tightened. These monsters were tougher than he expected.","And he didn’t have time to complain.","WHOOSH!","Something enormous came from his right.","Noah instinctively raised his sword.","CLANG!!","A massive paw smashed against the blade.","\"What the—?!\"","The sheer physical force overwhelmed him. Noah’s boots tore through the earth as he was thrown several meters backward.","Thud!","He struck the ground and rolled twice before forcing himself back onto one knee.","His arms trembled.","\"Damn...\"","His palms had gone numb. These bears weren’t individually terrifying.","The problem was their numbers.","ROOOAARRR!!","Another bear lunged at him.","Noah twisted sideways.","Four enormous claws passed inches from his face.","He immediately retaliated.","Swish!","His sword cut across the monster’s exposed side. Blood sprayed outward. But the wound wasn’t deep enough.","The bear spun around surprisingly quickly. Its paw slammed into Noah’s shoulder.","BAM!!","\"Argh!\"","Noah was sent staggering sideways. Pain exploded through his shoulder.","Before he could regain his footing. Another bear charged from behind.","His eyes widened.","\"Shit!\"","Noah threw himself forward.","BOOM!","The bear crashed into a tree instead.","The thick trunk cracked under the impact.","Noah rolled across the ground before immediately extending his left hand.","Mana surged.","CRACK!","Several thick ice spikes erupted beneath the bear. One pierced through its thigh.","\"GRRRAAAHHH!!\"","The monster roared violently.","Noah didn’t hesitate.","He dashed forward. His sword thrust directly through its open mouth.","SHLK!","The blade pierced through the back of its skull.","The bear’s body immediately went limp.","Noah pulled his sword free.","There was no time to breathe. Three more were already coming.","Noah retreated while observing their movements.","Don’t let them surround me.","That was the most important thing.","Nine opponents weren’t particularly dangerous if he use ice weapons. But he decided to go hard way.","Now if they surrounded him even with his superior speed, avoiding attacks from every direction would become difficult.","Noah suddenly turned and sprinted between two trees.","Exactly as expected the bears chased him.","Their large bodies forced them into a narrower formation.","A smile appeared on Noah’s face.","\"That’s better.\"","He abruptly stopped.","Turned.","His left foot planted firmly into the earth. Mana surged into his sword again.","Swish! Swish! Swish!","Three frost petals bloomed. The pale-blue crescents scattered apart.","The leading bears instinctively changed direction upon seeing them.","Exactly what Noah wanted.","The petals curved.","Not toward where the monsters were going. But toward where they had just been.","Two crescents crossed paths directly behind the leading bear.","BOOM!!","Frost erupted violently.","The explosion caught the second and third monsters charging behind it.","\"ROOOARRR!!\"","One was thrown sideways.","Another had both hind legs engulfed in rapidly expanding ice.","The frozen ground spread beneath them. Their movements became sluggish.","Noah’s eyes sharpened.","Now he charged.","His sword flashed.","Slash!","The first injured bear’s throat opened.","He stepped past it.","Rotated his wrist.","Slash!","His blade entered beneath the jaw of the second monster.","Blood sprayed across his clothes. The third attempted to strike him. Noah ducked beneath its paw.","Then stabbed upward.","SHLK!","His sword pierced directly through its chest.","The bear roared and attempted to crush him with both paws.","Noah immediately released his sword and jumped backward.","BAM!!","Its paws struck empty ground.","Noah raised his hand.","The sword embedded inside the bear’s chest suddenly became covered in frost.","Ice rapidly spread through the wound.","The monster staggered.","Then collapsed.","Noah breathed heavily.","\"Haa...\"","\"Haa...\"","His shoulder hurt.","There were claw marks across his clothes, and blood slowly trickled from a shallow wound along his upper arm.","His mana had also dropped considerably.","But when he looked ahead. Only four bears remained standing. Two were already injured. The largest one stepped forward.","Its crimson eyes stared at the corpses scattered across the frozen battlefield.","Then at Noah.","GRRRRRR...","Noah smirked. \"Let’s end this.\"","---","Just like that, five days passed.","Noah had spent those five days surviving alone in the forest—fighting and killing monsters, collecting their mana cores, and constantly pushing himself through one dangerous encounter after another.","For food, he roasted the meat of the monsters he killed or ate whatever edible fruits he could find.","At night, he usually slept high in the trees, where he was less likely to be attacked by monsters while resting.","But today, he discovered something different.","\"What is this?\"","Noah questioned curiously.","His master, Akari, had told him that she would come and find him after seven days, no matter where he ended up.","Because of that, Noah hadn’t paid much attention to which direction he was traveling.","And now, he had somehow stumbled upon a strange place.","It was a large, open circular space in the middle of the dense forest.","What made it unusual was the enormous circular stone platform covering the ground.","Around its edges stood several small stone pillars, each reaching roughly to his waist. Resting atop every pillar was a perfectly spherical red crystal.","Noah cautiously stepped onto the stone platform.","His eyes immediately fell upon the intricate patterns carved across its surface.","He crouched slightly and examined them more closely.","\"Not designs... Are these some kind of runes?\"","Noah couldn’t tell for certain.","Akari hadn’t mentioned anything about a place like this.","He slowly looked around at the red crystals surrounding the platform.","\"What could this be?\""]},{"number":270,"title":"Chapter 270: Training Ends","paragraphs":["\"Haa...\"","Noah lay sprawled across a huge rock, staring blankly at the sky above.","He looked absolutely miserable.","His clothes were torn and tattered, with scratches, cuts, and small wounds scattered across his body. Dried mud covered parts of his face, while dust clung to his hair and clothes.","He hadn’t taken a proper bath in the last four days.","\"...I’m done with this nonsense survival training.\"","He muttered lifelessly while continuing to stare at the sky.","The last sixteen days had been far more dangerous than the first five.","And for seven straight days, Noah had either been fighting or running for his life.","Sometimes, he genuinely felt that fighting monsters was the easier option compared to dealing with those strange plants.","Those things had tortured him in ways he didn’t even want to remember.","One had sprayed something that made his entire body itch for hours.","Another had nearly swallowed him whole.","Noah shuddered.","’Let’s not remember those.’","Akari had originally told him that the survival training would last for one week.","Seven days.Yet she hadn’t appeared after the seventh day. It had now been three entire weeks.","\"Oh my~ So you survived.\"","A sweet yet strangely chilling voice suddenly reached his ears.","Noah froze. Standing a short distance away was Akari.","She wore a dark-violet kimono that wrapped elegantly around her tall figure. Her raven-black hair was neatly arranged in its usual bun.","Noah’s exhausted eyes immediately lit up.","\"Akari...\"","His lips trembled. \"Oh, my Akari! You finally came!!\"","He hurriedly pushed himself upright on the rock.","\"Hey!\"","He pointed accusingly at her.","\"You were supposed to come after seven days! Seven! This was supposed to be seven days of survival training! Why did you suddenly increase it without even telling me?!\"","His expression looked genuinely betrayed.","Akari calmly stared at him.","\"Well, you were doing surprisingly well.\"","\"...\"","\"So I thought it would be beneficial if you continued for another week.\"","Noah stared at her. Then his shoulders suddenly trembled. He lowered his head.","\"Sniff...\"","Akari blinked.","\"Y-You...\"","His voice became shaky.","\"You-you should’ve at least told me that you were extending the training by another two weeks...\"","His voice sounded as though he were barely holding himself together.","Akari’s expression shifted.","\"Noah?\"","\"I-I thought...\"","He rubbed his eyes with the back of his hand.","\"I thought you suddenly decided to abandon me in some unknown forest because you got irritated with me...\"","\"What?\"","Akari’s eyes widened.","Noah’s shoulders trembled harder.","\"I-I know I’m annoying sometimes... and I tease you a lot...\"","He sniffled again.","\"So I thought maybe you finally got tired of me and decided not to come back...\"","He wiped his eyes again before any imaginary tears could fall.","\"I’m sorry if I really did something that upset you...\"","Akari’s entire expression changed.","\"N-Noah?!\"","She genuinely panicked.","Whoosh!","Her figure disappeared.","Before Noah could even react, Akari appeared beside him and immediately wrapped both arms around his body.","She pulled him firmly against herself.","Noah’s face pressed against her shoulder.","\"Noah, that’s not it!\"","Her usual calmness completely disappeared.","\"I would never abandon you! I simply thought extending your training would help you improve. I didn’t think you’d become this worried!\"","Her arms tightened around him.","\"I’m sorry, okay? I should’ve told you somehow.\"","She gently stroked his back.","\"I didn’t mean to make you feel abandoned.\"","Noah slowly wrapped his arms around her. He could feel her warmth against him.","Her genuine concern. Her arms holding him protectively.","And inwardly.","’Heh~’","Noah almost grinned.","’I’m pretty good at acting, aren’t I?’","He comfortably rubbed his cheek against Akari’s shoulder.","This was working far better than expecte.","’Wait.’","His eyes widened.","’My face. It was covered in dried mud. Even my whole body is dirty. I didn’t take any bath for three days. How did I forget?!’","Noah immediately pulled away, gently pushing Akari back.","\"Oh, damn! I forgot I’m filthy!\"","He quickly looked at the shoulder of her beautiful violet kimono.","\"Sorry, Akari. I got your clothes dirty.\"","\"Noah, it’s alright.\"","Akari was still worried about him.","\"This is nothing compared to how frightened you must have been when you thought I had abandoned—\"","She stopped.","\"...\"","Her eyes slowly moved toward Noah’s face.","She blinked.","Noah blinked back.","\"...\"","There wasn’t a single tear on his face. His eyes were perfectly clear. There was no water in his eyes.","Even his cheeks showed absolutely no sign that he had been crying.","Noah suddenly realized his mistake.","’...I got caught.’","A bead of imaginary sweat seemed to roll down his forehead.","’Shit!’","The warm, concerned expression on Akari’s face slowly disappeared. Her sapphire-blue eyes became cold.","Noah gulped.","\"H-Haha...\"","He scratched his cheek awkwardly.","\"Akari~\"","\"...\"","\"How was my acting?\"","Her eyebrow twitched.","\"I was just joking with yo—OUCH!!\"","Akari’s fingers suddenly caught his ear and twisted.","\"OW! OW! OW!\"","Noah immediately bent sideways.","\"Akari! That hurts!\"","\"Hmph!\"","She twisted harder.","\"I’m sorry! I’m sorry!\"","Noah frantically waved his hands.","\"I won’t do it again!\"","Akari refused to release him.","\"Do you have any idea how worried I became?!\"","\"Ow! Yes! Yes! I understand!\"","\"I genuinely thought I’d hurt you!\"","\"I’m sorry!\"","\"I thought you felt betrayed because of me!\"","\"Akari, my ear is going to come off!\"","\"Maybe it should!\"","\"Master, have mercy!\"","She finally released him after nearly a minute.","Noah immediately covered his aching ear.","\"Ow...\"","Akari crossed her arms.","\"Hmph!\"","She turned her face slightly away.","\"I became genuinely worried because I thought I’d hurt you, yet you were acting the entire time.\"","Her eyes returned to him.","Despite her glare, Noah could still see traces of concern within them.","\"Do you understand how terrible I felt when I thought you had spent an entire week believing I’d abandoned you?\"","Noah rubbed the back of his neck awkwardly.","\"Well...\"","His smile became apologetic.","\"Sorry.\"","Akari stared at him for several seconds.","Eventually, she released a long sigh.","\"Sigh... Fine.\"","Her shoulders relaxed.","\"I’ll forgive you.\"","Noah’s expression brightened.","\"Really?\"","\"Yes. Just don’t do something like that again.\"","\"Of course I won’t.\"","Akari narrowed her eyes.","\"Promise?\"","\"Promise.\"","\"Good.\"","Her expression finally softened.","Then she looked him over from head to toe.","\"And despite your ridiculous behavior...\"","A faint smile appeared on her lips.","\"You really did well during these two weeks.\"","Noah blinked.","Akari continued.","\"You survived entirely on your own. You fought monsters, found food, secured places to sleep, and adapted to unexpected dangers without anyone helping you.\"","There was unmistakable approval in her eyes.","\"If you were ever stranded somewhere alone in the future, I’m confident you’d be capable of surviving.\"","Noah smiled.","\"Well...\"","He proudly placed a hand against his chest.","\"I had an amazing master.\"","Akari’s lips curved slightly.","\"Flattery won’t make me forget what you just did.\"","\"Damn.\"","She shook her head helplessly.","Then Akari raised her right hand.","Noah watched curiously as she brought the long sleeve of her violet kimono toward his face.","She gently wiped his cheek.","Noah went still.","Akari carefully brushed away the dried mud and dust clinging to his skin. Her movements were slow and gentle.","\"Look at you...\"","She murmured.","\"Your entire face is covered with dirt.\"","Noah remained unusually quiet.","He simply allowed her to clean him.","Her expression was focused as she wiped the dirt from his cheek, then moved toward his forehead.","Noah watched her silently.","’She really cares about me...’","A small smile unconsciously appeared on his lips.","Something warm fluttered strangely within his stomach. It wasn’t because of her beauty. Nor because she was standing so close to him.","It was simply the tenderness behind such a small action.","For some reason having Akari quietly clean the dirt from his face made his heart feel strangely warm.","\"Well... I’m also sorry.\"","Akari’s expression softened as she looked at Noah.","\"I know you’re smart enough to understand that extending your training was something I did deliberately. I was watching you the entire time... Well, not exactly the entire time, but I checked on you every day and observed you until nightfall.\"","\"Hehe~ It’s alright.\"","Noah smiled at her.","\"I know you pretty well after spending so much time with you. No matter what happens, you wouldn’t abandon me. And if I were ever truly in life-threatening danger, you would’ve come to save me immediately.\"","A gentle smile appeared on Akari’s face.","\"You really are smart, aren’t you?\"","\"Of course I am.\"","Noah puffed out his chest proudly before chuckling.","\"And honestly, I didn’t mind doing the survival training for another week. Practical experience like this is much more useful than simply practicing techniques all day.\"","Akari’s smile widened.","She raised her hand and gently stroked his snow-white hair.","\"You’re suddenly saying so many sensible things that you’re making me happy.\"","\"Haha.\"","Noah didn’t know why bit in front of Akari he loves to act liked a spoiled child. It was kind of a fun.","Noah allowed her to stroke his head for a moment before suddenly remembering something.","\"Well, Akari... if you were watching me, then you probably saw me when I found that strange circular platform.\"","Akari’s hand paused.","\"Yes.\"","She slowly pulled her hand away.","Noah looked at her curiously.","\"So... what exactly is that place?\"","---","[A/N: Hello, guys!! I’ve uploaded Akari’s image to the character profile on the novel’s page. You can go check it out and give her some popularity in the rankings! Also, the image shows her without the scales on her neck and cheek.]"]},{"number":271,"title":"Chapter 271: Time For Reward","paragraphs":["\"I don’t know.\"","\"...You don’t know?\"","Noah raised an eyebrow.","\"Not even a small guess?\"","Akari shook her head.","\"No.\"","Her gaze drifted toward the distant forest as though recalling something from long ago.","\"When I first discovered that platform, I also thought it might have something to do with escaping this place. The strange carvings, those red crystals, the stone pillars... everything about it seemed unnatural.\"","She paused briefly.","\"I investigated it many times during my first few years here. I tried sending mana into the platform and the crystals. I examined the markings and searched the surrounding area for anything that might activate it.\"","\"And nothing happened?\"","\"Nothing.\"","Akari shook her head again.","\"For more than sixty years, that platform has remained exactly the same. Eventually, I stopped wasting my time trying to understand it.\"","Noah nodded slowly.","\"I see...\"","Yet his expression remained thoughtful.","\"But I still feel like there’s more to it.\"","Akari narrowed her eyes slightly.","\"Why do you think so?\"","\"I don’t really have a good reason.\"","Noah scratched his cheek.","\"It’s mostly a feeling. But those runes carved into the floor looked suspicious. Someone clearly built that platform for a purpose.\"","Akari remained silent for a moment.","\"Hmm...\"","Her expression became more serious.","\"You’re not wrong.\"","She glanced toward the forest.","\"Let’s discuss it properly once we return home.\"","\"Sure!\"","Noah pushed himself off the rock and stood.","Akari also stepped away from him.","Mana surged around her body.","A brilliant sapphire-blue glow enveloped her entire figure.","Noah instinctively stepped back as the mana surrounding her rapidly intensified.","Her silhouette expanded.","Her body transformed.","Within moments, the elegant woman in the violet kimono was gone.","In her place stood an enormous sapphire-scaled dragon.","Her massive wings unfolded above the forest, sending a powerful gust of wind through the surrounding trees.","Noah grinned.","No matter how many times he witnessed it, Akari’s transformation was still incredible.","He climbed onto her back and settled himself near the base of her neck.","\"Ready?\"","Akari’s deep voice rumbled through the air.","\"Ready!\"","Her enormous wings spread wide.","WHOOSH!!","With one powerful beat, Akari launched herself into the sky.","The forest rapidly shrank beneath them as she climbed higher, carrying Noah back toward the place that, without him realizing it, he had already begun thinking of home.","Once they finally returned home after such a long time, the first thing Noah did was take a proper bath.","After spending three weeks surviving in the forest, feeling clean again was almost heavenly.","He washed away the dried mud, sweat, and dust covering his body before carefully cleaning the small cuts and scratches he had accumulated during the training.","Afterward, he changed into a fresh set of clothes.","Noah had originally stored four sets of clothes inside his storage ring. Unfortunately, the ones he had worn during his survival training were now completely tattered and practically unusable.","That left him with only three sets.","Once he was ready, he walked into the living room.","Akari was already sitting there, waiting for him.","Her sapphire-blue eyes immediately moved across his body when he entered.","\"You’re finally freshened up.\"","\"Yep.\"","\"How are your wounds? Does your body still hurt?\"","Noah rotated his shoulder slightly before shaking his head.","\"I’m fine. They’re nothing serious.\"","Akari studied him for another moment before nodding.","\"Good.\"","She gestured for him to sit.","\"Now, let’s talk about that strange platform you discovered.\"","Noah was about to sit when something suddenly came to mind.","\"Wait.\"","Akari raised an eyebrow.","\"What?\"","\"Before that...\"","A mischievous smile slowly appeared on Noah’s face.","\"I want my reward.\"","\"...Reward?\"","Akari blinked.","Then realization appeared in her eyes.","\"Ah.\"","She chuckled softly.","\"That’s right. I completely forgot about it.\"","Noah sat down in front of her.","Akari smiled and asked, \"So, what do you want?\"","Then her eyes narrowed suspiciously.","\"And don’t ask me for anything ridiculous.\"","Noah’s smile widened.","\"Don’t worry. It’s something very simple.\"","That smile immediately made Akari even more suspicious.","\"...Why do I suddenly feel worried?\"","Noah ignored her comment.","\"Akari.\"","\"Hm?\"","He pointed toward his cheek.","\"As my reward...\"","Akari stared at his finger.","\"Give me a kiss on the cheek.\"","\"...\"","Silence.","Akari continued staring at him with the exact same gentle smile she had been wearing a moment ago.","Noah patiently waited.","\"...Noah.\"","\"Yes?\"","Her eyebrow twitched.","\"You said you wouldn’t ask for a kiss.\"","\"No, no.\"","Noah immediately raised one finger.","\"That’s not what I said.\"","Akari narrowed her eyes.","Noah continued confidently.","\"I said I wouldn’t ask you to let me kiss you.\"","He pointed toward himself.","\"Now I’m asking you to kiss me.\"","\"...\"","Akari’s lips pressed tightly together.","A faint pink blush slowly appeared across her otherwise composed face.","\"You...\"","She stared at him incredulously.","\"You deliberately worded it that way?\"","Noah gave her an innocent smile.","\"Maybe?\"","Akari closed her eyes.","\"This shameless boy...\"","\"I survived for weeks alone because of your training!\"","\"That doesn’t mean—\"","\"I fought monsters!\"","\"Noah—\"","\"I nearly got eaten by giant flowers!\"","\"You survived perfectly well.\"","Noah placed a hand dramatically against his chest.","\"After everything your poor disciple suffered through, Master won’t even give him one tiny reward?\"","Akari stared at him.","\"No.\"","Her answer was immediate.","Noah’s expression collapsed.","\"Why?!\"","\"Because it’s embarrassing!\"","The words escaped her mouth before she could stop herself.","Akari froze.","Noah blinked.","A second later, his eyes sparkled.","\"So you don’t actually hate the idea.\"","Akari’s blush deepened.","\"That’s not what I said!\"","\"But you said it’s embarrassing. You didn’t say you don’t want to.\"","\"Noah!\"","\"Hehe~\"","Akari turned her face away from him with a frustrated sigh.","\"I won’t do it.\"","She continued staring outside, deliberately refusing to look at him.","Then she made the mistake of glancing back.","Noah was staring at her with wide, pleading blue eyes. His lips were slightly pursed, his expression carrying the most pitiful look he could possibly manage.","Akari immediately looked away again.","’Don’t look at him.’ She thought.","Her fingers tightened slightly over her kimono."]},{"number":272,"title":"Chapter 272: Reward~","paragraphs":["Noah continued his little act.","\"Master... please...\" he pleaded, making his expression as pitiful as possible. \"Just once. I really want it... Or do you actually hate me? Maybe you find me disgus—\"","\"Fine! Fine! You win!\"","Akari finally snapped.","She turned toward him with a furious glare, but the soft blush spreading across her cheeks completely ruined the intimidating expression she was trying to make.","Noah’s eyes immediately brightened.","Akari crossed her arms and huffed. \"Hmph! I never thought you’d turn out like this. You were such a sweet young man when we first met.\"","\"Hehe~ Now you understand that I’m just like any other man.\"","Noah gave her a mischievous smile.","\"Tch!\"","Akari looked away.","\"Other young men at least wouldn’t ask such things from an old lady.\"","Noah raised an eyebrow.","\"Shouldn’t something like this be normal for you? I’m just a kid in your eyes, aren’t I?\"","Akari immediately turned and glared at him.","\"But with the way you’ve been flirting with me lately, it’s becoming difficult to think of you as—\"","She abruptly stopped. Her eyes widened slightly.","\"F-Forget it!\"","She quickly turned her face away again.","Noah stared at her for a moment. Then his smile grew wider.","He wisely chose not to tease her about what she had nearly said. Instead, he slid across the wooden floor until he was sitting directly in front of her, much closer than before.","\"Alright.\"","He straightened his back proudly.","\"It’s finally time to receive the reward for my three weeks of brutal training.\"","Akari sighed helplessly.","\"...Okay.\"","She closed her eyes for a moment and took a slow breath, trying to calm herself.","’It’s only a kiss on the cheek.’","There was nothing strange about it. Nothing embarrassing. At least, that was what she repeatedly told herself.","Noah leaned forward and turned his head slightly, presenting his cheek to her.","\"Here.\"","\"...\"","Akari stared at his cheek. Her fingers unconsciously tightened against the fabric of her kimono.","Noah waited patiently.","Akari inhaled quietly.","Then she leaned forward. The distance between them disappeared.","Chuu~","Her soft pink lips gently pressed against Noah’s cheek. Noah froze. Despite all his teasing and confidence from only moments ago, the instant he actually felt her lips against his skin, his mind became strangely blank.","Warm. That was his first thought. Her lips were incredibly soft and warm against his cheek.","Ba-dump.","His heart suddenly beat harder.","Ba-dump. Ba-dump.","A warm sensation spread through his chest. Without realizing it, Noah’s eyes slowly closed. A genuine smile appeared on his face.","Akari didn’t immediately move away either. Her lips remained against his cheek for several quiet seconds. For those few seconds, neither of them spoke.","Then Akari finally pulled away.","Noah slowly opened his eyes.","His smile remained.","\"Akari, that was—\"","Crackle!","\"...Huh?\"","Blue lightning suddenly erupted around Akari’s body. Before Noah could finish his sentence.","WHOOSH!","She disappeared. A streak of blue lightning shot through the open veranda and vanished into the forest.","Noah remained sitting there. He was motionless. His mouth was still slightly open.","\"...\"","Silence filled the room.","He blinked once.","\"Pfft—\"","His shoulders began trembling.","\"Hahaha!\"","Noah fell backward onto the wooden floor, laughing. \"Hahahaha! She actually ran away!\"","He covered his eyes with one hand, unable to stop himself.","’She’s becoming cuter and cuter with each passing day.’","Eventually, his laughter subsided. Noah raised his other hand and gently touched the cheek Akari had kissed.","A soft smile returned to his face. \"That was nice.\"","He continued rubbing the spot absentmindedly for another moment. Then he glanced toward the empty veranda.","\"But she really left...\"","His smile became helpless. \"We were supposed to talk about that strange circular platform.\"","Noah sighed and stretched himself out across the wooden floor. His arms moved behind his head as he stared lazily at the wooden ceiling.","\"Well...\"","He had nowhere else to go. \"I’ll just wait for her to come back.\"","His fingers briefly touched his cheek again. A small grin returned.","\"...Worth it.\"","---","After a while.","\"Cough! Cough!\"","Akari once again sat in front of Noah. She coughed few times to clear her throat.","She had returned after nearly fifteen minutes—apparently, that was how long she needed to calm herself down.","Her posture was perfectly straight, her hands resting neatly over her lap. Her expression had returned to its usual cold and indifferent state, as though absolutely nothing embarrassing had happened earlier.","Unfortunately for her the tips of her ears were still as red as tomatoes.","Noah noticed them immediately. His lips threatened to curve upward, but he wisely controlled himself.","Akari narrowed her eyes at him. \"Don’t bring up that topic.\"","Her voice was calm but carried a clear warning. \"Let’s talk about important things now.\"","\"Yes.\"","Noah nodded obediently. Then his expression gradually became serious.","\"But before that, there’s something else I want to tell you.\"","Akari raised an eyebrow.","\"What is it?\"","\"I want to tell you everything that has happened to me at the academy over the past four months.\"","His playful expression completely disappeared. \"I think it’s important that you know. Honestly, I should’ve told you all of this much earlier.\"","Akari observed him for a moment before nodding.","\"Then tell me now.\"","Her expression softened slightly.","\"We have plenty of time.\"","Noah nodded.","\"Alright.\"","He adjusted his sitting position before taking a breath. Then he began from the beginning.","He told her about the first incident that had happened after he entered the academy.","Until now, Noah had never explained everything to Akari in detail. Their days together had mostly been consumed by training, meditation, survival exercises.","And, admittedly, Noah spending far too much time teasing and flirting with her.","But now that they were seriously decided to discuss the mysterious platform. But befroe that he told her what incidents and dangers had had went through. Noah realized there was no reason to hide anything from her.","If anything, Akari might notice something he had overlooked. So Noah talked. And talked.","For more than an hour, his voice continued throughout the quiet wooden house.","He explained everything in as much detail as he could remember—the incidents at the academy, the dangers he and his classmates had encountered, the strange events surrounding him and Damien, and everything else that had happened during those chaotic four months.","Akari didn’t interrupt unnecessarily. She simply listened.","At first, her expression remained calm.","Occasionally, she asked a short question whenever Noah mentioned something unclear, but otherwise she allowed him to continue at his own pace.","However, as the story progressed. Her expression slowly changed. The faint amusement that had remained in her eyes disappeared completely. Her gaze became sharper.","Her posture grew increasingly rigid.","And by the time Noah had gone through most of what had happened over the last four months."]},{"number":273,"title":"Chapter 273: Eternal Monarchs","paragraphs":["\"You really have gone through a lot in just a few months.\"","Akari spoke after remaining silent for a moment.","\"Yes...\"","Noah gave a helpless sigh.","Akari lowered her gaze, carefully organizing everything he had told her.","\"Hmm... So, according to your theory, the reason you were brought here has something to do with Damien?\"","\"Yes.\"","Noah nodded.","\"You believe that stone slab activated the portal because Damien’s blood spilled onto it?\"","\"Exactly.\"","His expression turned serious.","\"As I mentioned before, Damien is blessed by the Sun God. And I’m not talking about the way people casually use the word blessed.\"","Akari quietly listened.","\"Sometimes, when someone is born with an extraordinary innate ability or possesses an unusually powerful talent, people say that person has been ’blessed by the gods.’ But that’s mostly just an expression.\"","Noah shook his head.","\"Damien is different.\"","His blue eyes narrowed.","\"He is genuinely blessed by the Sun God. If you want to put it another way... I suppose you could call him a child favored by the heavens.\"","Akari remained silent for several seconds.","\"What you’re saying does make sense.\"","She slowly nodded.","\"After hearing about everything that happened involving you and Damien, even I can tell that there’s something extraordinary surrounding him.\"","Her expression gradually became more serious.","\"Which means...\"","She paused.","\"Noah, you’re suggesting that Damien was the person who was originally supposed to be brought here.\"","Noah nodded.","\"Yes.\"","\"But because you were standing beside the stone slab when the portal activated...\"","\"I got dragged inside instead.\"","Silence settled between them.","Akari released a long sigh. \"This has become far more complicated than I expected.\" She looked toward the open veranda. \"If someone truly blessed by the Sun God has appeared in future era...\"","Her sapphire-blue eyes narrowed. \"...then the Monarchs may soon return as well.\"","Noah immediately frowned. \"Monarchs?\"","Akari looked back at him.","\"What do you mean by Monarchs?\"","She remained silent for a moment. Her expression suggested that she was considering whether she should tell him at all.","Eventually, she sighed. \"This isn’t information someone at your current level would normally be allowed to learn.\"","Noah straightened slightly.","\"But considering everything you’ve already become involved in...\"","Akari shook her head.","\"Keeping you ignorant might be more dangerous.\"","She looked directly into his eyes.","\"In this world, ancient records speak of two kinds of existences that once stood above nearly everything else.\"","She raised two fingers.","\"The first were the Eternal Gods.\"","Her second finger remained raised.","\"And the others were the Eternal Monarchs.\"","Noah’s expression changed slightly.","\"Eternal Monarchs...\"","\"Yes.\"","Akari nodded.","\"Calling them simply Gods and Monarchs doesn’t properly describe what they were. According to ancient records, both stood at heights that ordinary beings couldn’t even comprehend.\"","\"How powerful?\"","Akari’s expression became solemn.","\"Powerful enough to destroy entire worlds.\"","Noah’s eyes widened.","\"...What?\"","\"At least, that’s what the surviving ancient texts claim.\"","Akari quickly added the clarification.","\"There are records describing beings capable of destroying worlds, reshaping them, and, at their absolute peak, possessing enough power to bring ruin to an entire world easily.\"","Noah remained silent.","He had already seen enough impossible things since arriving in this world that he couldn’t simply dismiss such claims as myths.","\"So the Eternal Gods are stronger than the Monarchs?\"","\"No.\"","Akari shook her head.","\"That’s what makes them frightening.\"","She paused.","\"The Eternal Monarchs were supposedly capable of standing against the Eternal Gods as equals.\"","Noah’s expression grew more serious.","\"Then what’s the difference between them?\"","\"The nature of their powers.\"","Akari raised her hand slightly.","\"The Gods wield divine power. Their strength is closely associated with divinity, faith, prayers, worship, and the beliefs of their followers.\"","\"And the Monarchs?\"","\"That’s where the records become unclear.\"","Akari frowned.","\"I’ve never found a reliable explanation of exactly what kind of energy the Monarchs wielded.\"","She thought for a moment before continuing.","\"However, their powers were frequently associated with things that ancient civilizations considered dangerous or unnatural.\"","\"Such as?\"","\"Blood.\"","Akari raised one finger.","\"Flesh.\"","Another.","\"Death, Souls, Darkness, Decay, Destruction... and several other concepts.\"","Noah listened carefully.","\"Because of that, Monarchs were generally portrayed as evil beings?\"","\"Yes. At least in eyes of mortals.\"","Akari nodded.","\"And in the records I’ve read.\" She then immediately added, \"But I wouldn’t blindly trust those descriptions.\"","Noah raised an eyebrow.","\"Why?\"","\"Because history is written by people.\"","Akari’s gaze became thoughtful.","\"And people are biased.\"","She rested her hands over her lap.","\"Most surviving records concerning the Eternal Gods were preserved by temples, churches, kingdoms that worshipped them, or scholars living under civilizations devoted to them.\"","Noah immediately understood her point.","\"So if the Gods and Monarchs were enemies...Then naturally, records written by followers of the Gods would portray the Monarchs as monsters.\"","Akari nodded.","\"That doesn’t mean the Monarchs were innocent. They may genuinely have been horrifying beings. But we don’t know enough to say that every Eternal God was good and every Eternal Monarch was evil.\"","\"History could have been distorted.\"","\"Exactly. And don’t you find it weird? That there is only one god worshiped by most kingdoms. The Sun God. There is barely any information about other gods. Even the statue you saw underground, calling it moon goddess.\"","She paused and continued. \"I never have heard about such goddess before.\"","Noah fell into thought.","That explanation made far more sense to him than simply dividing beings of unimaginable power into good gods and evil monarchs.","Akari continued.","\"Still, one thing appears repeatedly throughout ancient records.\"","\"What?\"","\"When beings heavily favored by the Eternal Gods begin appearing in the world...\"","Her eyes narrowed.","\"...the influence of the Eternal Monarchs eventually follows.\"","Noah’s expression stiffened.","Immediately, several memories resurfaced.","Noah looked at Akari.","\"Then Marbas...\"","\"That’s exactly what I was thinking.\"","Akari’s expression darkened.","\"You said Marbas, that demon attempted to sacrifice numerous students to an unknown entity.\"","\"Yes.\"","\"We don’t know what that entity was.\" Akari shook her head. \"But considering what you’ve told me, there’s a possibility that it was connected to an Eternal Monarch.\"","Noah frowned.","\"Connected how?\"","\"A follower. A servant. Someone attempting to get their favor. Someone borrowing its power.\"","She paused.","\"Or perhaps something even worse.\"","Noah understood immediately.","\"The Monarch itself.\"","\"Possibly.\"","Akari didn’t sound certain.","\"We simply don’t have enough information.\"","She then continued.","\"And there’s another incident that concerns me even more.\"","\"The dungeon?\"","\"Yes.\"","Akari’s gaze sharpened.","\"You said someone spoke through the body of the creature you and Damien defeated.\"","Noah nodded.","\"And whoever it was immediately recognized Damien as someone blessed by the Sun God.\"","\"Exactly.\"","\"That’s not ordinary knowledge, Noah.\"","Akari’s voice became noticeably colder.","\"Even powerful people might fail to recognize a true divine blessing without investigating Damien carefully. Yet this unknown being recognized it almost immediately.\"","Noah slowly clenched his hand.","\"So whoever spoke through that corpse... May possess knowledge dating back to the Eternal Gods and Monarchs.\"","Akari nodded.","\"It could be a follower of a Monarch.\"","Her eyes narrowed.","\"Or...\"","Noah finished the thought himself.","\"...an Eternal Monarch.\"","Neither spoke for several moments. Noah’s expression had become extremely serious. Then another thought suddenly crossed his mind.","Something Akari had said earlier.","Noah knew that this games would have eternal monarchs and gods. But what they were exactly, he didn’t know. Even Akari knew all of this because she was daughter of one of the power house of kingdom. Also wife of a duke.","Then Noah’s eyes slowly widened. His own status appeared within his thoughts.","Bloodline: [Monarch of the Frost]","\"...\"","Noah suddenly became very quiet.","’That means... I really have chance to become strong... like eternal monarchs. Who are as strong as Gods.’"]},{"number":274,"title":"Chapter 274: Akari You Are The Best!!","paragraphs":["It was exciting and dangerous at the same time.","The more Noah learned about the forces moving behind the scenes, the more complicated everything became.","Akari remained silent for a moment before sighing.","\"Honestly, I have no idea what’s happening in the outside world anymore.\"","Her expression became thoughtful.","\"The dragon who trapped me here may have deliberately created that labyrinth to bring Damien to this place. But why?\"","She narrowed her eyes.","\"Did he want something from Damien? Or perhaps—\"","\"Damien was the key to getting you out of this place.\" Noah finished her sentence.","Akari looked at him.","\"...Perhaps.\"","Noah lowered his gaze. Unlike Akari, he already knew something she didn’t. Or at least, he believed he did.","Noah have no knowledge of the game. So he had speculate this things.","’But instead of Damien...’","Noah clenched his hands slightly.","’I was the one who got dragged here.’ His expression gradually darkened. ’And I don’t even know how to get her out.’","A bitter feeling settled inside his chest. It wasn’t an emotion Noah experienced very often. But this time, he genuinely felt guilty.","Akari had spent sixty years trapped here. Sixty years alone. And perhaps, after all that time, the person capable of finally freeing her had arrived only for Noah to accidentally take his place.","’Shit.’","Noah stared at the wooden floor.","’If Damien was really supposed to help her escape, then she must be disappointed. Instead of someone who could save her...She got me.’","Suddenly something warm wrapped around his shoulders.","\"...Hm?\"","Before Noah could react, he was gently pulled sideways. His face came to rest against Akari’s shoulder.","She had wrapped an arm around his back and pulled him into a warm embrace.","Noah blinked. Her other hand settled atop his snow-white hair. She began gently stroking his head.","\"What happened?\"","Her voice was soft.","\"You suddenly became so gloomy.\"","Noah remained silent.","Akari looked down at him.Then a knowing smile appeared on her lips. Her cold expression changed.","\"Hehe~ Don’t tell me...\"","Her fingers continued moving gently through his hair. \"Are you feeling guilty because you came here instead of Damien?\"","Noah stiffened.","\"Yes.\"","He couldn’t lie to her about that.","\"I mean...\"","His voice became quieter.","\"If Damien really was supposed to come here, then maybe he was supposed to help you escape.\"","Noah’s arms rested loosely beside him. \"But instead, I came here. And I don’t know how to get you out.\"","He frowned. \"So maybe—\"","\"We don’t know that.\"","Akari immediately interrupted him.","Noah looked up slightly.","She stared down at him with calm sapphire-blue eyes.","\"You don’t know the future, Noah.\"","Her fingers gently brushed through his hair.","\"Neither do I.\"","\"But—\"","\"Just because Damien may have been the person intended to arrive here doesn’t mean he was destined to free me.\"","Noah became quiet.","Akari continued.","\"For all we know, that dragon might have wanted to lure Damien here for an entirely different reason.\"","Her expression became serious.","\"Perhaps he wanted Damien’s help. Or his power. Or something connected to his blessing.\"","Her eyes narrowed.","\"Or perhaps his intentions toward Damien were far more sinister than either of us currently realizes.\"","Noah slowly relaxed. That was true. Everything he currently believed was based on his intuition. But this world had already deviated from what one could know.","Far too many things had happened differently. At least that what Noah believed. His assumptions weren’t absolute facts.","\"And besides...\"","Akari’s voice became gentler. Noah felt her arm tighten slightly around him.","\"I would never feel sad or disappointed because you came here instead of Damien.\"","Noah’s eyes widened slightly.","Akari smiled.","\"I’m happy that it was you.\"","Something warm bloomed inside Noah’s chest. His arm slowly moved around her waist.","\"Really?\"","\"Really.\"","Akari nodded.","Noah couldn’t stop himself from asking.","\"Why?\"","Akari thought for a moment.","\"After everything you’ve told me about Damien, he sounds like a good young man.\"","\"He is.\"","\"But...\"","A hint of amusement appeared in her eyes.","\"I don’t think I would’ve become this close to him.\"","Noah’s smile slowly returned.","\"Oh?\"","\"Yes.\"","Akari chuckled softly.","\"We probably would’ve maintained a much more respectful relationship.\"","She looked down at the young man currently comfortably resting against her.","\"A proper relationship between master and disciple.\"","Then her eyes narrowed playfully.","\"Unlike a certain disciple of mine who is far too mischievous, shameless, and naughty.\"","Noah grinned.","\"Hehe~ So you prefer your naughty disciple?\"","Akari’s eyebrow twitched.","\"Don’t twist my words.\"","\"Haha!\"","The gloomy feeling that had weighed upon Noah only moments earlier disappeared. His grip around her became slightly firmer.","\"We’ll find a way out.\"","His voice suddenly became serious again.","Akari looked at him.","Noah raised his head from her shoulder and met her eyes. \"We’ll find a way out of this place together.\"","His blue eyes carried genuine determination.","\"No matter how difficult it is. No matter how long it takes. We’ll find a way.\"","Akari silently stared at him. Then her expression softened.","\"Yes.\"","She nodded.","\"We will.\"","A peaceful silence followed. Then Akari smiled. \"And even if we don’t...It wouldn’t be so terrible anymore.\"","\"What?\"","Akari’s hand returned to his hair. Her fingers gently stroked through the snowy strands.","\"I’ve already spent sixty years here, Noah.\"","Her gaze became distant for a moment.","\"Back then, the thought of remaining trapped here forever terrified me.\"","She paused. \"But now...\"","Her eyes returned to him.","There was unmistakable warmth within them. \"I’m not alone anymore.\"","Noah froze.","\"...\"","His lips trembled. Something squeezed tightly inside his chest.","\"Akari...\"","Then he suddenly wrapped both arms tightly around her.","\"Ah!\"","Akari gasped in surprise.","\"Noah?\"","\"Akari!!\"","He squeezed her tighter.","\"You’re the best!\"","\"Noah—\"","\"You’re seriously the best!\"","Akari blinked before eventually realizing why he had suddenly become so joyful.","A helpless smile appeared on her face.","\"Calm down.\"","\"No!\"","Noah buried his face against her shoulder.","\"Let me stay like this!\"","Akari laughed softly.","\"Hehe. Very well.\"","Her arms wrapped around him again. She gently stroked his back while allowing him to cling to her. Noah could feel her warmth against him, but for once, his mind didn’t wander anywhere inappropriate.","He was simply happy. Happy that she wasn’t disappointed. Happy that she didn’t wish Damien had come instead. And most of all happy that his presence had made sixty years of loneliness a little easier for her.","Akari rested her cheek gently against his snow-white hair.","\"You really are troublesome, Noah.\"","Her voice carried no annoyance. Only warmth. Noah smiled against her shoulder.","\"Hehe~\"","Akari’s smile widened.","\"But...\"","Her arms tightened around him slightly.","\"I suppose I’ve gotten used to having my troublesome disciple around.\"","---","[A/N: Damn it! Every day, I tell myself, \"Yes, this will be the last Chapter focused on romance, and then I’ll finally start the real action!\" But somehow, I fail every single time. Seriously, I’m starting to think I should just write a damn romance-focused novel someday. Maybe a rom-com? Yeah, I might actually try that in the future. Anyway, this time I’ll move things along faster... Yep! No more sweet moments!!","...Probably.]"]},{"number":275,"title":"Chapter 275: Aura","paragraphs":["Six Months Later","The forest remained exactly as it had been when Noah first arrived. Beautiful and peaceful.","The crystal-clear lake still reflected the sky like a giant mirror, while the dense forest surrounding it swayed gently beneath the breeze.","Birds chirped among the branches, and the occasional rustling of leaves revealed small animals moving through the undergrowth.","Yet while the forest hadn’t changed much, Noah certainly had.","More than six months had passed since he had been dragged into this strange world.","Looking back, the time almost felt like it had disappeared in the blink of an eye.","Most of his days had been spent training under Akari—practicing his swordsmanship, fighting monsters, meditating, improving his control over mana, and occasionally attempting to understand the mysteries surrounding this place while strengthening his ice creation ability.","And today was no different.","In the spacious yard outside the wooden house, Noah stood with a sword firmly gripped in his right hand.","His breathing was slow and controlled.","A faint azure glow surrounded his body.","But unlike ordinary training, his attention was entirely focused on the blade in his hand.","Hum—","Mana flowed from his core.","Azure energy traveled through his arm before pouring into the sword.","Normally, a person would simply coat their weapon in mana. Such reinforcement increased the weapon’s durability and destructive power, allowing even an ordinary blade to withstand far greater force than it normally could.","But Noah was attempting something far more advanced. He wasn’t merely covering the sword with mana. He was compressing it. More and more.","The azure mana surrounding the blade gradually condensed.","Noah narrowed his eyes.","Controlling mana in this manner required tremendous precision. If the flow became unstable, the compressed energy would simply disperse.","If he forced too much mana into one section, the coating would become uneven and collapse.","He had struggled with exactly that problem for months.","At first, he couldn’t maintain the shape for even a second.","Then it became three seconds.","Five.","Ten.","And as his control improved, the unstable layer of mana slowly began taking on a more defined form.","The azure glow surrounding the sword intensified.","Noah carefully compressed the mana along the edge of the blade, forcing the normally fluid energy into something denser. He tried to shape the mana into something sharp and solid.","The vague blue glow slowly transformed.","A thin, solid-looking layer of brilliant azure energy formed around the sword.","Its edges were frighteningly sharp.","The air around the blade seemed to tremble faintly as the concentrated energy distorted it.","Noah’s lips curled upward.","\"...There.\"","He raised the sword.","Unlike ordinary mana reinforcement, which merely strengthened the weapon, this technique transformed mana itself into an extension of the blade.","Sharper and denser and far more destructive.","Noah turned toward a nearby tree.","Its trunk was thick enough that he would’ve needed several ordinary swings to cut through it completely.","He stepped forward.","Then swung.","Slash—!","There was almost no resistance.","The azure-coated blade passed cleanly through the thick trunk.","For a brief moment, nothing happened.","Then—","Creak...","The upper half of the tree slowly tilted sideways.","THUD!","It crashed heavily against the ground, shaking the earth and scattering leaves everywhere.","Noah stared at the perfectly smooth cut left behind on the stump.","His grin widened.","\"Damn...\"","He raised his sword and examined the brilliant azure edge.","\"It’s as sharp as ever.\"","Far sharper than simply coating his weapon with ordinary mana.","And there was a reason for that.","What surrounded Noah’s blade wasn’t ordinary mana anymore.","It was Aura.","After months of relentless practice under Akari’s guidance, Noah had finally learned how to manifest it.","Aura was created by taking mana, controlling it with extreme precision, compressing it far beyond ordinary reinforcement, and shaping that condensed energy around a weapon—or even the user’s own body.","It was like advance version of normal mana strengthening around weapons or body.","Rather than merely strengthening a sword, Aura effectively created an additional supernatural edge around it.","That was why the tree had offered almost no resistance.","However Noah watched the azure coating carefully.","Crackle—","A tiny portion of the Aura flickered.","Then destabilized.","\"Tch.\"","Noah immediately reduced the mana flowing into the blade.","The brilliant coating gradually disappeared.","He exhaled slowly. He had learned Aura.","But he was still far from mastering it.","Maintaining such highly compressed mana required constant concentration, and the technique consumed considerably more energy than ordinary reinforcement.","During an actual battle, Noah couldn’t keep his entire sword covered in Aura indefinitely.","Not yet, anyway.","But six months ago, he couldn’t even create it.","Now he could maintain a stable blade of Aura long enough to use it effectively in combat.","And weapons weren’t its only application.","Once his control improved further, Noah could coat parts of his own body with Aura as well.","His fists. His arms. His legs.","Potentially even his entire body.","Compared to ordinary mana enhancement, the resulting increase in offensive power and defense would be on an entirely different level.","Aura was mostly learned by those people who dedicated themselves for weapons and martial arts. Not focusing on magic.","It takes long time for one to learn. But because Noah having Adaptive Learbing, which helps him to adapt to things easily.","He learned this faster. Where it had take him more than a year, he learned it in half year.","Noah stared at the fallen tree before looking down at his sword.","Noah stared at the fallen tree for a moment before lowering his gaze to the sword in his hand.","Then, without hesitation, he moved.","He dashed through the surrounding trees, his sword flowing through the air like water. A brilliant blue trail followed the blade with every swift swing.","Slash! Slash! Slash!","Each strike sliced cleanly through a tree trunk with almost no resistance.","One after another, the trees were severed as though his blade were cutting through butter.","A satisfied smirk appeared on his face.","\"Not bad.\"","He lightly swung the blade through the air.","\"But it’s still nowhere near Akari’s level. It will take decade for me to reach that level.\"","And that alone reminded him just how much further he still had to climb.","’Status’","The moment he thought about status, a translucent floating screen appeared in front of him.","=== STATUS ===","Name: Noah Eldritch","Race: Human","Age: 19 Years","Strength: 612 [+244]","Speed: 617 [+253}","Stamina: 619 [+247]","Endurance: 608 [+249]","Charm: 700","Mana: 6213 [+2679]","Core Rank: Condensed (Mid)","Potential: Mythical Core / Origin Core (???)","Profession: [Combatant Lv.3]","Technique: [Frozen Lotus Blade Art], [Flowing String Archery]","Affinity: Ice","Spells: [Ice Shard], [Frost Bind], [Snow Mist], [Ice Blizzard], [Crystal Bloom], [Winter Howl]","Innate Ability: [Ice Creation]","Passive Abilities: [Adaptive Learning], [Heart of Absolute Frost]","Active Ability: [Monarch’s Decree]","Bloodline: [Monarch of the Frost]","==================="]}]);
